(window.STEP_BOOK = window.STEP_BOOK || {})["G4"] = {"n":4,"level":"B2","t":"Complex Time, Conditions and Reporting","lessons":[{"id":"4.1","t":"Narrative Tenses, Including the Past Perfect Continuous","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.1 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Combine the past simple, past continuous, past perfect and past perfect continuous in narratives.</p>\n<p>2. Use the past perfect continuous for duration before a point in the past.</p>\n<p>3. Choose the correct tense from time markers (by the time, had been … for, just as, when).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يجمع الطالب بين الماضي البسيط والمستمر والتام والتام المستمر في السرد.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يستخدم الماضي التام المستمر للتعبير عن مدة سابقة لنقطة في الماضي.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يختار الزمن الصحيح من مؤشرات الزمن مثل by the time وhad been … for وjust as.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. She was exhausted because she ______ all night.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. studied B. has studied</p>\n<p>C. had been studying D. was study</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Just as I ______ the house, it started to rain.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. left B. had been leaving</p>\n<p>C. have left D. leave</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. By the time the ambulance arrived, the man ______ consciousness.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. has lost B. lost already C. was losing D. had lost</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Past simple</strong></p>\n<p><strong>main completed events in order</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He opened the door, looked around and walked in.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Past continuous</strong></p>\n<p><strong>was / were + -ing — background, interrupted action</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. It was getting dark and the wind was blowing.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Past perfect</strong></p>\n<p><strong>had + past participle — completed earlier action</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. When we arrived, the guests had left.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Past perfect continuous</strong></p>\n<p><strong>had been + -ing — duration / activity up to a past moment</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She had been waiting for two hours when the bus came.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Time markers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>by the time · before · after · when · as soon as · just as · while · for / since (with past perfect)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. By the time I found my keys, the taxi had gone.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Result clues</strong></p>\n<p><strong>tired / wet / dirty / red eyes … because … had been + -ing</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. His clothes were dirty because he had been fixing the car.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Telling a story in order.</strong></p>\n<p>The past simple moves the story forward; the other tenses give background and earlier information.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Last summer we drove to Abha. The road was climbing through the mountains and fog was covering the valleys.</p>\n<p>▸ We stopped at a small café that my father had visited years before.</p>\n<p>▸ The owner had been working there for forty years and still remembered him.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Past perfect continuous for duration before a past moment.</strong></p>\n<p>It shows how long an activity continued before something else happened.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ They had been living in Tabuk for ten years when they moved to Riyadh.</p>\n<p>▸ I had been studying for three hours when the power went off.</p>\n<p>▸ How long had you been waiting when the doctor called you?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Past perfect continuous to explain a past result.</strong></p>\n<p>It explains why something looked or felt a certain way in the past.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The ground was wet. It had been raining all night.</p>\n<p>▸ Omar was out of breath because he had been running.</p>\n<p>▸ Her eyes were red; she had been crying.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Past perfect simple vs continuous.</strong></p>\n<p>Simple stresses the completed result or number; continuous stresses the activity and its duration.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ By noon, she had written three reports. (completed, number)</p>\n<p>▸ By noon, she had been writing reports for four hours. (duration)</p>\n<p>▸ By the time the match ended, the team had scored four goals.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Stative verbs (know, believe, own, belong) use the past perfect simple, not continuous: We had known each other for years.</p>\n<p>▸ Do not overuse the past perfect: if the order is clear from before / after, the past simple is often enough.</p>\n<p>▸ just as = at exactly the moment when: Just as I sat down, the phone rang.</p>\n<p>▸ had been + -ing is the same for all subjects.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في السرد نستخدم الماضي البسيط للأحداث الرئيسة المتتابعة، والماضي المستمر للخلفية أو للحدث الذي قُطع، والماضي التام للحدث الذي وقع قبل غيره في الماضي.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الماضي التام المستمر يتكون من had been مع الفعل المنتهي بـ ing، ونستخدمه للتعبير عن نشاط استمر مدة معينة قبل لحظة في الماضي، أو لتفسير نتيجة ظاهرة في الماضي مثل التعب أو البلل.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نستخدم الماضي التام المستمر مع أفعال الحالة مثل know وown، ونستخدم بدلًا منه الماضي التام البسيط.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She was tired because she has been working all day.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She was tired because she had been working all day.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في سياق الماضي نستخدم had been لا has been.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>We had been knowing them for years.</em> <strong>→ ✓ We had known them for years.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">know فعل حالة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>When I arrived, they already left.</em> <strong>→ ✓ When I arrived, they had already left.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحدث الأسبق في الماضي التام.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I had been wait for an hour.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I had been waiting for an hour.</strong></p>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">had been + ing.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He had been written three letters.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He had written three letters.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع العدد والنتيجة المكتملة الماضي التام البسيط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>While I walked home, I was seeing an accident.</em> <strong>→ ✓ While I was walking home, I saw an accident.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحدث الطويل مستمر والقصير بسيط.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Past continuous: At 9 p.m. I was studying. (in progress at that time)</p>\n<p>Past perfect: I had studied before I went to bed. (completed earlier)</p>\n<p>Past perfect continuous: I had been studying for three hours when my friend called. (duration up to then)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Find the reference point in the past (when …, by the time …).</p>\n<p>2. Earlier and completed → had + p.p.; earlier and continuing for a time → had been + -ing.</p>\n<p>3. for + period before a past event → past perfect continuous.</p>\n<p>4. Result visible in the past (wet, tired, dirty) → had been + -ing.</p>\n<p>5. Stative verbs → simple forms only.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد نقطة الإسناد في الماضي، فإذا كان الحدث سابقًا ومكتملًا فالماضي التام، وإذا كان سابقًا ومستمرًا مدة فالماضي التام المستمر، وتذكّر أفعال الحالة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The workers ______ for six hours when they finally took a break.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. worked B. were working</p>\n<p>C. had been working D. have been working</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> for six hours shows duration.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The duration was before a past moment (they took a break).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Past perfect continuous. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مدة قبل لحظة ماضية: had been working.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. By the time I got to the stadium, the first half ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. had finished B. has finished</p>\n<p>C. was finishing D. had been finish</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> By the time + past simple (got).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The first half finished before that moment → completed earlier.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Past perfect. The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحدث الأسبق المكتمل: had finished.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. His (A) <u>hands</u> were black (B) <u>because</u> he (C) <u>has been</u> (D) <u>fixing</u> the car.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. hands B. because C. has been D. fixing</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The story is in the past (were).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The earlier ongoing activity explains a past result → had been.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: His hands were black because he had been fixing the car. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في سياق الماضي had been لا has been.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 D · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 A · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"When I opened the door, I realized that someone ______ in.","o":["has broken","broke in already","had broken","was breaking"],"k":2,"e":"Earlier completed action → past perfect.","h":"الحدث الأسبق المكتمل."},{"n":2,"s":"We ______ for an hour when the guide finally arrived.","o":["have been waiting","had been waiting","were waited","waited since"],"k":1,"e":"Duration before a past moment → past perfect continuous.","h":"مدة قبل لحظة ماضية."},{"n":3,"s":"It ______ heavily, so the roads were flooded.","o":["has been raining","rains","had rain","had been raining"],"k":3,"e":"Earlier ongoing activity explaining a past result.","h":"تفسير نتيجة ماضية."},{"n":4,"s":"Just as we ______ dinner, the lights went out.","o":["had been starting","have started","start","started"],"k":3,"e":"just as + main event → past simple.","h":"just as مع الماضي البسيط."},{"n":5,"s":"She was nervous because she ______ in public before.","o":["has never spoken","had never spoken","never speaks","had never been speaking"],"k":1,"e":"Experience before a past moment → past perfect simple.","h":"تجربة قبل لحظة ماضية."},{"n":6,"s":"While the students ______ the test, the fire alarm rang.","o":["were taking","took","had taken","take"],"k":0,"e":"Interrupted action → past continuous.","h":"حدث مستمر قُطع."},{"n":7,"s":"By the time the police arrived, the thieves ______.","o":["have escaped","had escaped","escaped already","were escape"],"k":1,"e":"By the time → past perfect.","h":"By the time مع الماضي التام."},{"n":8,"s":"Fahad's eyes were tired because he ______ at the screen all day.","o":["had been looking","has been looking","looks","had looked at"],"k":0,"e":"Duration explaining a past result → had been + -ing.","h":"تفسير نتيجة ماضية."},{"n":9,"s":"They ______ each other for twenty years when they started the company.","o":["had been knowing","have known","knew since","had known"],"k":3,"e":"know is stative → past perfect simple.","h":"know فعل حالة."},{"n":10,"s":"I ______ home when I saw an old friend from school.","o":["was walking","walked","had walked","had been walk"],"k":0,"e":"Background action interrupted → past continuous.","h":"حدث خلفي مقطوع."},{"n":11,"s":"How long ______ been living in Dammam before you moved to Jeddah?","o":["have you","had you","did you","were you"],"k":1,"e":"Duration before a past event → had you been.","h":"مدة قبل حدث ماضٍ."},{"n":12,"s":"When I reached the shop, I found that I ______ my wallet at home.","o":["have left","was leaving","had been leaving","had left"],"k":3,"e":"Earlier completed action → had left.","h":"حدث أسبق مكتمل."},{"n":13,"s":"By noon, Huda ______ three chapters of her new novel.","o":["had been writing","has written","had written","was writing"],"k":2,"e":"A completed number → past perfect simple.","h":"النتيجة المكتملة بالعدد."},{"n":14,"s":"The old man told us that he ______ as a fisherman for forty years.","o":["has worked","had worked","works","is working"],"k":1,"e":"Reported duration in the past → past perfect.","h":"مدة في الماضي المنقول."},{"n":15,"s":"We were surprised to see the streets so busy; the festival ______ that morning.","o":["has started","had started","starts","had been start"],"k":1,"e":"Earlier event → past perfect.","h":"حدث أسبق."},{"n":16,"s":"The children were covered in sand because they ______ on the beach all afternoon.","o":["have been playing","played since","had been playing","had play"],"k":2,"e":"Activity with duration explaining a past result.","h":"نشاط مستمر يفسر النتيجة."},{"n":17,"s":"Before he became a teacher, my father ______ in a bank.","o":["had worked","has worked","works","was work"],"k":0,"e":"Earlier period in the past → past perfect.","h":"فترة سابقة."},{"n":18,"s":"I was so tired that I fell asleep while I ______ the film.","o":["had been watched","watched","have watched","was watching"],"k":3,"e":"Background action → past continuous.","h":"حدث خلفي."},{"n":19,"s":"She ______ the piano for ten years before she gave her first concert.","o":["had been practising","has been practising","practises","was practise"],"k":0,"e":"Duration up to a past event → past perfect continuous.","h":"مدة قبل حدث ماضٍ."},{"n":20,"s":"When the plane finally took off, we ______ on the runway for nearly two hours.","o":["were sitting since","have been sitting","had sit","had been sitting"],"k":3,"e":"Duration before the take-off → had been sitting.","h":"مدة قبل الإقلاع."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"I (A) was (B) exhausted because I (C) have been (D) travelling all day.","o":["was","exhausted","have been","travelling"],"k":2,"e":"Past context → had been.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"When we (A) arrived, the (B) meeting (C) already (D) started.","o":["arrived","meeting","already","started"],"k":2,"e":"Earlier action → had already started.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"They (A) had been knowing each (B) other (C) since (D) childhood.","o":["had been knowing","other","since","childhood"],"k":0,"e":"know is stative.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"He (A) had (B) been (C) work in the garden for hours, so he (D) was hungry.","o":["had","been","work","was"],"k":2,"e":"had been + -ing.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) While I (B) walked (C) along the beach, I (D) found a strange shell.","o":["While","walked","along","found"],"k":1,"e":"Background action with while → past continuous.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"By the (A) time the firefighters (B) came, the (C) building (D) has burned down.","o":["time","came","building","has burned"],"k":3,"e":"By the time → had burned.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"(A) She had been written five emails (B) by the time her (C) manager (D) arrived.","o":["She had been written","by","manager","arrived"],"k":0,"e":"A completed number → past perfect simple.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"The (A) streets were (B) wet because it (C) rained (D) all night.","o":["streets","wet","rained","all"],"k":2,"e":"Earlier ongoing activity explaining a past result.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"Just (A) as the (B) teacher (C) entered, the students (D) had stood up.","o":["as","teacher","entered","had stood"],"k":3,"e":"Two events at the same moment → past simple.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"How (A) long (B) have you been (C) waiting when the bus (D) came?","o":["long","have","waiting","came"],"k":1,"e":"Duration before a past event → had.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"4.2","t":"Future Continuous and Future Perfect","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.2 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Form the future continuous for actions in progress at a future time.</p>\n<p>2. Form the future perfect (simple and continuous) for completion or duration by a future time.</p>\n<p>3. Use by, by the time, this time next week and in … time accurately.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكوّن الطالب المستقبل المستمر لحدث سيكون مستمرًا في وقت ما في المستقبل.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يكوّن المستقبل التام البسيط والمستمر للتعبير عن الاكتمال أو المدة قبل وقت مستقبلي.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم by وby the time وthis time next week استخدامًا دقيقًا.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. This time tomorrow, I ______ on the beach in Yanbu.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. will lie B. will be lying C. will have lain D. lie</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. By 2030, they ______ the new airport.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. will build B. will be building</p>\n<p>C. build D. will have built</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. By June, I ______ English for six years.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. will have been studying B. will study</p>\n<p>C. am studying D. studied</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Future continuous</strong></p>\n<p><strong>will be + verb-ing</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. At 8 p.m. tomorrow I will be flying to Cairo.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Future continuous — negative / question</strong></p>\n<p><strong>won't be + -ing · Will + subject + be + -ing …?</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Will you be using the car tonight?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Future perfect simple</strong></p>\n<p><strong>will have + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. By Friday we will have finished the project.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Future perfect — negative / question</strong></p>\n<p><strong>won't have + p.p. · Will + subject + have + p.p. …?</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Will they have arrived by six?</em></p>\n<p><strong>Future perfect continuous</strong></p>\n<p><strong>will have been + verb-ing (+ for …)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. By December she will have been working here for ten years.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Time expressions</strong></p>\n<p><strong>this time next week · at 10 a.m. tomorrow · by + time · by the time + present simple · in two years' time</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. By the time you get home, I'll have cooked dinner.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Future continuous: an action in progress at a specific future time.</strong></p>\n<p>We imagine ourselves in the middle of the action at that time.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ At nine tomorrow morning, I'll be sitting my STEP test.</p>\n<p>▸ Don't call at 7; we'll be having dinner.</p>\n<p>▸ This time next month, my brother will be studying in London.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Future continuous: planned or routine future events; polite questions.</strong></p>\n<p>It sounds natural and polite for plans.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The plane will be landing in Riyadh in twenty minutes.</p>\n<p>▸ Will you be going to the supermarket later? Could you buy some bread?</p>\n<p>▸ I'll be seeing Ahmed at the meeting anyway, so I'll give him the file.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Future perfect: completed before a future time.</strong></p>\n<p>We look back from a point in the future.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ By the end of this year, the metro will have opened all its lines.</p>\n<p>▸ I will have saved enough money by the summer.</p>\n<p>▸ By the time you arrive, the film will have started.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Future perfect continuous: duration up to a future point.</strong></p>\n<p>It shows how long something will have continued by a certain time.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Next month my grandfather will have been working on his farm for fifty years.</p>\n<p>▸ By 5 p.m. we will have been driving for eight hours.</p>\n<p>▸ In June, I will have been learning English for ten years.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ After by the time / when / before (future), use the present simple: By the time you arrive, … (not will arrive).</p>\n<p>▸ by = not later than: by Friday, by 2030, by the end of the month.</p>\n<p>▸ Stative verbs are not used in the continuous forms: By June I will have known her for a year.</p>\n<p>▸ will have + p.p. — never will have + past simple: ✗ will have went.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المستقبل المستمر يتكون من will be مع الفعل المنتهي بـ ing، ونستخدمه لحدث سيكون في منتصفه في وقت محدد في المستقبل، مثل This time tomorrow I'll be flying.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المستقبل التام يتكون من will have مع التصريف الثالث، ونستخدمه لحدث سيكتمل قبل وقت محدد في المستقبل، ويأتي غالبًا مع by وby the time.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المستقبل التام المستمر يتكون من will have been مع ing، ويعبّر عن مدة نشاط مستمر حتى نقطة في المستقبل. وبعد by the time نستخدم المضارع البسيط لا will.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>This time tomorrow I will travel to Cairo.</em> <strong>→ ✓ This time tomorrow I will be travelling to Cairo.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدث مستمر في وقت مستقبلي محدد.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>By Friday I will finish the report.</em> <strong>→ ✓ By Friday I will have finished the report.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الاكتمال قبل وقت مستقبلي يحتاج المستقبل التام.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>By the time you will arrive, we will have eaten.</em> <strong>→ ✓ By the time you arrive, we will have eaten.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد by the time المضارع البسيط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She will have went home by then.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She will have gone home by then.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">التصريف الثالث gone.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>By June I will have been knowing her for a year.</em> <strong>→ ✓ By June I will have known her for a year.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">know فعل حالة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I will be finish at five.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I will be finishing at five. / I will have finished by five.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">will be + ing أو will have + p.p.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Future continuous: At 6 p.m. I'll be cooking. (in the middle of it)</p>\n<p>Future perfect: By 6 p.m. I'll have cooked dinner. (finished before 6)</p>\n<p>Future perfect continuous: By 6 p.m. I'll have been cooking for two hours. (duration)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. at + future time / this time next … → future continuous.</p>\n<p>2. by + future time / by the time … → future perfect.</p>\n<p>3. by … + for + period → future perfect continuous.</p>\n<p>4. No will after by the time / when / before in the time clause.</p>\n<p>5. Check participles after will have (gone, written, built).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع وقت محدد في المستقبل يكون الحدث فيه مستمرًا استخدم will be + ing، ومع by وby the time للاكتمال استخدم will have + التصريف الثالث، ومع المدة استخدم will have been + ing.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Don't phone me at 10 tonight. I ______ my favourite programme.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. will watch B. will be watching</p>\n<p>C. will have watched D. watch</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> at 10 tonight = a specific future time.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> I will be in the middle of watching → future continuous.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدث مستمر في وقت محدد: will be watching.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. By the time we get to the party, everyone ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. will leave B. will be leaving</p>\n<p>C. leaves D. will have left</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> By the time + present simple (get).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Leaving will be completed before that time.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Future perfect. The answer is D.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">اكتمال قبل وقت مستقبلي: will have left.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>By</u> next July, my parents (B) <u>will</u> (C) <u>be</u> married (D) <u>since</u> twenty-five years.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. By B. will C. be D. since</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> twenty-five years is a period.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> A period needs for, not since.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: By next July, my parents will have been married for twenty-five years. The answer is D.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع المدة for لا since.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 D · 3 A · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 D · Example 3 D","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"This time next week, we ______ in the mountains of Asir.","o":["will be hiking","will hike","will have hiked","hike"],"k":0,"e":"this time next week → future continuous.","h":"this time next week مع المستمر."},{"n":2,"s":"By 2030, Riyadh ______ many new parks.","o":["will be building","builds","will built","will have built"],"k":3,"e":"by 2030 → future perfect.","h":"by مع المستقبل التام."},{"n":3,"s":"At 9 a.m. tomorrow, I ______ my driving test.","o":["will take on","will be taking","will have taken","take"],"k":1,"e":"at + future time → in progress → future continuous.","h":"حدث مستمر في وقت محدد."},{"n":4,"s":"By the end of this month, I ______ this whole book.","o":["will be reading","will read","read","will have read"],"k":3,"e":"by the end of → future perfect.","h":"by the end of مع المستقبل التام."},{"n":5,"s":"By next year, my uncle ______ in this company for twenty years.","o":["will work","is working","will have been working","will be work"],"k":2,"e":"Duration up to a future point → future perfect continuous.","h":"مدة حتى نقطة مستقبلية."},{"n":6,"s":"______ you be using your laptop this evening? I need to borrow it.","o":["Will","Do","Are","Have"],"k":0,"e":"Polite future continuous question → Will you be using …?","h":"سؤال مهذب بالمستقبل المستمر."},{"n":7,"s":"By the time you ______ this message, I will have left.","o":["will read","read","will have read","are reading by"],"k":1,"e":"After by the time → present simple.","h":"بعد by the time المضارع."},{"n":8,"s":"Don't wait for me. I ______ late at the office tonight.","o":["will have worked","work","worked","will be working"],"k":3,"e":"Planned activity in progress tonight → future continuous.","h":"نشاط مخطط ومستمر."},{"n":9,"s":"The plane ______ in Jeddah in about twenty minutes.","o":["will have landed since","will be landing","lands at","landed"],"k":1,"e":"Scheduled event in progress soon → future continuous.","h":"حدث مجدول."},{"n":10,"s":"Will the builders ______ the bridge by December?","o":["have finished","be finish","finished","have finish"],"k":0,"e":"Future perfect question: Will … have + p.p.?","h":"سؤال المستقبل التام."},{"n":11,"s":"In two years' time, Sara ______ from university.","o":["will be graduating since","will have graduated","graduates","has graduated"],"k":1,"e":"Completed by a future time → future perfect.","h":"اكتمال قبل وقت مستقبلي."},{"n":12,"s":"When you arrive at the airport, I ______ for you at the gate.","o":["will be waiting","will have waited","wait","am waited"],"k":0,"e":"Action in progress at a future moment → future continuous.","h":"حدث مستمر عند وصولك."},{"n":13,"s":"By 10 p.m., we ______ for twelve hours without a break.","o":["will have been driving","will drive","will be drive","have driven"],"k":0,"e":"Duration up to a future time → future perfect continuous.","h":"مدة حتى وقت مستقبلي."},{"n":14,"s":"I'm sure she ______ her exams by the time we visit her.","o":["will be finishing","finishes","will have finished","will finished"],"k":2,"e":"Completed before a future event → future perfect.","h":"اكتمال قبل حدث مستقبلي."},{"n":15,"s":"Next Ramadan, my grandparents ______ married for sixty years.","o":["will be being","are","will have","will have been"],"k":3,"e":"State duration up to a future point → will have been (stative be).","h":"حالة حتى نقطة مستقبلية."},{"n":16,"s":"At this time tomorrow, the team ______ the final match.","o":["will be playing","will have played since","plays","will play at"],"k":0,"e":"In progress at a future time → future continuous.","h":"حدث مستمر."},{"n":17,"s":"By the end of the course, you ______ over 500 new words.","o":["will have learned","will be learning","learn","will learning"],"k":0,"e":"Completed amount by a future time → future perfect.","h":"العدد المكتمل."},{"n":18,"s":"Please don't call between 2 and 4; I ______ a lecture.","o":["will give at","will be giving","will have given","give"],"k":1,"e":"In progress during a future period → future continuous.","h":"حدث مستمر خلال فترة."},{"n":19,"s":"By the time the guests come, my mother ______ the food.","o":["will prepare","will be prepare","will have prepared","prepares"],"k":2,"e":"Completed before the guests come → future perfect.","h":"اكتمال قبل قدوم الضيوف."},{"n":20,"s":"By next summer, I ______ Hessa for ten years.","o":["will have been knowing","will know since","will have known","know"],"k":2,"e":"know is stative → future perfect simple.","h":"know فعل حالة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"This time (A) tomorrow I (B) will sit in the (C) exam (D) hall.","o":["tomorrow","will sit","exam","hall"],"k":1,"e":"In progress at a future time → will be sitting.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"By the (A) time you (B) get here, we (C) will (D) finish dinner.","o":["time","get","will","finish"],"k":3,"e":"Completed before → will have finished.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"(A) By the time you will arrive, the (B) shops (C) will have (D) closed.","o":["By the time you will arrive","shops","will have","closed"],"k":0,"e":"After by the time → present simple.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"By 2035, (A) scientists (B) will (C) have find a cure for (D) many diseases.","o":["scientists","will","have find","many"],"k":2,"e":"will have + past participle found.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) By June, I (B) will have (C) been studying English (D) since eight years.","o":["By","will have","been studying","since"],"k":3,"e":"A period → for.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"Will (A) you (B) using the (C) car (D) tonight?","o":["you","using","car","tonight"],"k":1,"e":"Future continuous question: Will … be + -ing?","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"Next month, my (A) father (B) will have (C) been knowing his best friend (D) for forty years.","o":["father","will have","been knowing","for"],"k":2,"e":"know is stative.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"(A) Don't visit at six; (B) we (C) will be (D) pray Maghrib.","o":["Don't","we","will be","pray"],"k":3,"e":"will be + -ing.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"By (A) then, the (B) workers (C) will have went (D) home.","o":["then","workers","will have went","home"],"k":2,"e":"will have + gone.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"At (A) midnight, most (B) people in the city (C) will (D) sleeping.","o":["midnight","people","will","sleeping"],"k":3,"e":"will be + -ing.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"4.3","t":"Third and Mixed Conditionals; unless, provided that, as long as, in case","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.3 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Form third conditionals for unreal past situations.</p>\n<p>2. Build mixed conditionals that link the past and the present.</p>\n<p>3. Use unless, provided (that), as long as and in case with the correct tense.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكوّن الطالب الجملة الشرطية الثالثة للمواقف غير الحقيقية في الماضي.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يبني الجمل الشرطية المختلطة التي تربط الماضي بالحاضر.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم unless وprovided that وas long as وin case مع الزمن الصحيح.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. If I had known about the party, I ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. would come B. will come</p>\n<p>C. would have come D. came</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. If she ______ harder, she would have passed.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. had studied B. studied C. would study D. has studied</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Take a jacket ______ it gets cold.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. unless B. in case C. as long as D. provided</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Third conditional</strong></p>\n<p><strong>If + past perfect, would / could / might + have + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. If you had told me, I would have helped you.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Mixed: past condition → present result</strong></p>\n<p><strong>If + past perfect, would + base verb (now)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Mixed: present condition → past result</strong></p>\n<p><strong>If + past simple, would have + p.p.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. If I weren't so shy, I would have spoken to him yesterday.</em></p>\n<p><strong>unless = if … not</strong></p>\n<p><strong>unless + present (real) · unless + past (unreal)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We'll miss the bus unless we hurry.</em></p>\n<p><strong>provided (that) / as long as = only if</strong></p>\n<p><strong>provided that / as long as + present simple, will …</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. You can borrow my car as long as you drive carefully.</em></p>\n<p><strong>in case = because it is possible that</strong></p>\n<p><strong>… in case + present simple (precaution)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I'll take some water in case I get thirsty.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Third conditional: imagining a different past.</strong></p>\n<p>The situation did not happen; we imagine the result.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ If we had left earlier, we wouldn't have missed the flight. (We left late and missed it.)</p>\n<p>▸ She would have won the race if she hadn't fallen.</p>\n<p>▸ If you had asked me, I could have helped you.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Mixed conditionals: past cause, present result (and the reverse).</strong></p>\n<p>We connect a past situation with a present result, or a present fact with a past result.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ If I had saved more money last year, I would have a car now.</p>\n<p>▸ If my father hadn't moved to Riyadh, I wouldn't be studying here today.</p>\n<p>▸ If he weren't afraid of flying, he would have come to Dubai with us.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. unless, provided that, as long as.</strong></p>\n<p>unless = except if; provided / as long as = on condition that.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ You won't improve unless you practise every day.</p>\n<p>▸ You can go to the camp provided that your parents agree.</p>\n<p>▸ As long as you return it by Sunday, you can borrow my book.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. in case: a precaution.</strong></p>\n<p>in case is NOT the same as if: we do something now because something might happen.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Take your passport in case they ask for ID.</p>\n<p>▸ I saved his number in case I need help.</p>\n<p>▸ Bring an umbrella in case it rains. (Take it now — it may rain.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ No would in the if-clause: ✗ If I would have known …</p>\n<p>▸ Contractions: I'd have = I would have; if I'd known = if I had known.</p>\n<p>▸ in case + present simple even for the future: in case it rains (not in case it will rain).</p>\n<p>▸ unless already contains not: ✗ unless you don't hurry.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة الشرطية الثالثة تتكون من If مع الماضي التام، ثم would have مع التصريف الثالث، وتعبّر عن موقف لم يحدث في الماضي ونتيجته المتخيلة، مثل If you had told me, I would have helped you.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الجملة المختلطة تربط شرطًا ماضيًا بنتيجة حاضرة: If + الماضي التام ثم would مع الفعل الأصلي، أو شرطًا حاضرًا بنتيجة ماضية.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">unless تعني «إلا إذا»، وprovided that وas long as تعنيان «بشرط أن»، أما in case فتعني «تحسّبًا لـ» ونستخدمها للاحتياط، ويأتي بعدها المضارع البسيط.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>If I would have known, I would have come.</em> <strong>→ ✓ If I had known, I would have come.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا would في جملة الشرط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>If she had studied, she would passed.</em> <strong>→ ✓ If she had studied, she would have passed.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">النتيجة would have + p.p.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Unless you don't hurry, you'll be late.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Unless you hurry, you'll be late.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">unless تحمل النفي.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Take an umbrella in case it will rain.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Take an umbrella in case it rains.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد in case المضارع البسيط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>If I had studied medicine, I would have been a doctor now.</em> <strong>→ ✓ If I had studied medicine, I would be a doctor now.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع now تكون النتيجة حاضرة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I will lend you my car as long as you will drive carefully.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I will lend you my car as long as you drive carefully.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد as long as المضارع.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Second: If I had a car, I would drive. (present, unreal)</p>\n<p>Third: If I had had a car, I would have driven. (past, unreal)</p>\n<p>Mixed: If I had bought a car last year, I would drive to work now.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Look at the time: past situation that didn't happen → third conditional.</p>\n<p>2. If the result has now / today / still → mixed (would + base).</p>\n<p>3. No will / would after if, unless, provided, as long as, in case.</p>\n<p>4. in case = precaution (do it now); if = condition.</p>\n<p>5. Check have + past participle after would / could / might in the result.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذا كان الموقف في الماضي ولم يحدث فاستخدم الشرطية الثالثة، وإذا ظهرت كلمة now في النتيجة فهي مختلطة، ولا تضع will أو would بعد if وunless وin case.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. If the driver had been more careful, the accident ______.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. wouldn't happen B. won't happen</p>\n<p>C. wouldn't have happened D. didn't happen</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> had been → the condition is about the past.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Past unreal result → would have + p.p.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرط ماضٍ غير حقيقي: wouldn't have happened.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. If I hadn't missed the bus this morning, I ______ so tired now.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. wouldn't have been B. won't be</p>\n<p>C. wouldn't be D. hadn't been</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Condition: past (this morning). Result: now.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Past condition → present result: would + base.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرط ماضٍ ونتيجة حاضرة: wouldn't be.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. Take some (A) <u>snacks</u> (B) <u>in case</u> you (C) <u>will get</u> hungry (D) <u>on</u> the trip.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. snacks B. in case C. will get D. on</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> in case is followed by the present simple.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> will get → get.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: Take some snacks in case you get hungry on the trip. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد in case المضارع البسيط.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 C · 2 A · 3 B · Worked examples: Example 1 C · Example 2 C · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"If you had told me earlier, I ______ you.","o":["would help","will help","would have helped","had helped"],"k":2,"e":"Third conditional result.","h":"نتيجة الشرطية الثالثة."},{"n":2,"s":"If we ______ the map, we wouldn't have got lost.","o":["took","had taken","would take","have taken"],"k":1,"e":"Third conditional if-clause → past perfect.","h":"جملة الشرط بالماضي التام."},{"n":3,"s":"You won't pass the STEP ______ you practise regularly.","o":["if","in case","unless","provided"],"k":2,"e":"Won't pass except if you practise → unless.","h":"unless = إلا إذا."},{"n":4,"s":"Take your phone ______ you need to call me.","o":["unless","as long as","provided","in case"],"k":3,"e":"Precaution → in case.","h":"احتياط in case."},{"n":5,"s":"If I had gone to bed earlier, I ______ so tired now.","o":["wouldn't have been","won't be","wouldn't be","am not"],"k":2,"e":"Past condition, present result (now) → would + base.","h":"شرط ماضٍ ونتيجة حاضرة."},{"n":6,"s":"You can stay out late ______ you call us.","o":["unless","as long as","in case","although"],"k":1,"e":"On condition that → as long as.","h":"بشرط as long as."},{"n":7,"s":"She ______ the job if she had applied on time.","o":["might get","might have got","may get","had got"],"k":1,"e":"Third conditional result with might.","h":"might have + p.p."},{"n":8,"s":"If he hadn't eaten so much, he ______ sick last night.","o":["wouldn't have felt","wouldn't feel","won't feel","hadn't felt"],"k":0,"e":"Third conditional (last night).","h":"الشرطية الثالثة."},{"n":9,"s":"I'll lend you the money ______ you pay me back next week.","o":["unless","in case","provided that","even if"],"k":2,"e":"On condition → provided that.","h":"بشرط provided that."},{"n":10,"s":"If they ______ about the traffic, they would have taken the metro.","o":["had known","knew","would know","have known"],"k":0,"e":"Third conditional if-clause.","h":"جملة الشرط بالماضي التام."},{"n":11,"s":"If I were braver, I ______ to the manager yesterday.","o":["would speak","would have spoken","will speak","had spoken"],"k":1,"e":"Present condition, past result → would have + p.p.","h":"شرط حاضر ونتيجة ماضية."},{"n":12,"s":"I'll write the number down ______ I forget it.","o":["unless","in case","provided","as long as"],"k":1,"e":"Precaution → in case.","h":"احتياط."},{"n":13,"s":"If my parents hadn't moved to Jeddah, I ______ Arabic so fluently today.","o":["wouldn't speak","wouldn't have spoken","won't speak","didn't speak"],"k":0,"e":"Past condition, present result (today).","h":"نتيجة حاضرة."},{"n":14,"s":"______ you hurry, you'll miss the start of the film.","o":["If","As long as","In case","Unless"],"k":3,"e":"Except if you hurry → Unless.","h":"إلا إذا."},{"n":15,"s":"If you ______ me, I could have picked you up from the airport.","o":["had called","called","would call","have called"],"k":0,"e":"Third conditional if-clause.","h":"الماضي التام في الشرط."},{"n":16,"s":"We would have enjoyed the trip more if it ______ so hot.","o":["wasn't","hadn't been","wouldn't be","isn't"],"k":1,"e":"Third conditional (past) → hadn't been.","h":"الماضي التام المنفي."},{"n":17,"s":"You can use my laptop ______ you don't install any games.","o":["unless","in case","although","as long as"],"k":3,"e":"On condition → as long as.","h":"بشرط."},{"n":18,"s":"If she had followed the doctor's advice, she ______ healthy now.","o":["would have been","will be","is","would be"],"k":3,"e":"Past condition, present result.","h":"شرط ماضٍ ونتيجة حاضرة."},{"n":19,"s":"Bring warm clothes ______ the nights are cold in the desert.","o":["unless","provided","in case","as long as"],"k":2,"e":"Precaution → in case.","h":"احتياط."},{"n":20,"s":"Had I known about the meeting, I ______ it.","o":["would attend","will attend","had attended","would have attended"],"k":3,"e":"Inverted third conditional (Had I known = If I had known).","h":"الشرطية الثالثة المقلوبة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"If I (A) would have known the answer, I (B) would have (C) told (D) you.","o":["would have known","would","told","you"],"k":0,"e":"No would in the if-clause.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"If she (A) had left (B) earlier, she (C) wouldn't miss the (D) train.","o":["had","earlier","wouldn't miss","train"],"k":2,"e":"Third conditional result → would have missed.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"We (A) can go (B) camping this weekend (C) as long as the weather (D) will be good.","o":["can","camping","as long as","will be"],"k":3,"e":"After as long as → present simple.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"Unless (A) you (B) don't leave now, (C) you'll miss (D) the bus.","o":["you","don't leave","you'll","the"],"k":1,"e":"unless already means if not.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"If he (A) had (B) saved his money, he (C) would have had a car (D) now.","o":["had","saved","would have had","now"],"k":2,"e":"Present result (now) → would have (mixed conditional).","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"(A) In case you finish your homework, you (B) can (C) watch TV (D) tonight.","o":["In case","can","watch","tonight"],"k":0,"e":"This is a condition, not a precaution → If.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"We (A) would have (B) won the match if our best player (C) hadn't (D) been injure.","o":["would have","won","hadn't","been injure"],"k":3,"e":"been + past participle injured.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"If I (A) had (B) study harder last year, I (C) would be at university (D) now.","o":["had","study","would be","now"],"k":1,"e":"had + past participle studied.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) Had I knew about the delay, I (B) would have (C) stayed (D) home.","o":["Had I knew","would","stayed","home"],"k":0,"e":"Had + subject + past participle known.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"My (A) father lent me his car (B) provided that I (C) will return it (D) by nine.","o":["father","provided that","will return","by"],"k":2,"e":"Past context; no will after provided that → returned.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"4.4","t":"wish, if only, would rather, it's time","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.4 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Express regret about the past with wish / if only + past perfect.</p>\n<p>2. Express annoyance or a desired change with wish + would.</p>\n<p>3. Use would rather and it's (high) time + past simple.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يعبّر الطالب عن الندم على الماضي باستخدام wish وif only مع الماضي التام.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يعبّر عن الانزعاج أو الرغبة في التغيير باستخدام wish مع would.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم would rather وit's (high) time مع الماضي البسيط.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. I wish I ______ harder for the test last week.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. studied B. had studied C. would study D. study</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. I'd rather ______ at home tonight.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. to stay B. staying C. stayed D. stay</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. It's time we ______ home. It's very late.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. went B. go C. will go D. had gone</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>wish / if only + past simple (present)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>wish + subject + past simple / were / could</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I wish I knew the answer. If only I were taller!</em></p>\n<p><strong>wish / if only + past perfect (past regret)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>wish + subject + had + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I wish I had listened to my teacher.</em></p>\n<p><strong>wish + would (annoyance / desired change)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>wish + another person / thing + would + base verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I wish my brother would stop shouting.</em></p>\n<p><strong>would rather + base verb (same subject)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + would rather ('d rather) + base verb (+ than + base verb)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I'd rather walk than take a taxi.</em></p>\n<p><strong>would rather + past simple (different subject)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + would rather + another subject + past simple</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I'd rather you didn't tell anyone.</em></p>\n<p><strong>it's (high / about) time + past simple</strong></p>\n<p><strong>It's time + subject + past simple · It's time + to + verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. It's time we left. It's high time you started revising.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Regrets about the past.</strong></p>\n<p>We wish the past had been different, but it can't change.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I wish I had brought my camera to AlUla.</p>\n<p>▸ If only we hadn't missed the last bus!</p>\n<p>▸ She wishes she had accepted the scholarship.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Wishes about the present.</strong></p>\n<p>We want the present situation to be different.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I wish I lived closer to school.</p>\n<p>▸ If only I could speak Japanese!</p>\n<p>▸ My sister wishes she weren't so busy.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. wish + would: annoying habits and things we want others to change.</strong></p>\n<p>We use it for other people or things, not for ourselves.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I wish the neighbours would turn their music down.</p>\n<p>▸ I wish it would stop raining.</p>\n<p>▸ My mother wishes my brother would tidy his room.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. would rather and it's time.</strong></p>\n<p>would rather = prefer; it's time + past simple = it should happen now (it's a little late).</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I'd rather have tea than coffee, please.</p>\n<p>▸ My father would rather we stayed at home tonight.</p>\n<p>▸ It's high time the city built more parks.</p>\n<p>▸ It's about time you got a new phone!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Do not use wish + would for yourself: ✗ I wish I would be rich. ✓ I wish I were rich.</p>\n<p>▸ If only is stronger and more emotional than I wish.</p>\n<p>▸ would rather + base verb (no to): ✗ I'd rather to stay.</p>\n<p>▸ It's time + to + verb is neutral (It's time to go); It's time + past simple suggests we are late.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للتعبير عن الندم على الماضي نستخدم wish أو if only مع الماضي التام، مثل I wish I had studied، وللتعبير عن أمنية في الحاضر نستخدم الماضي البسيط أو were أو could.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم wish مع would للتعبير عن الانزعاج من عادة شخص آخر أو الرغبة في أن يتغير شيء، ولا نستخدمها مع ضمير المتكلم نفسه.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">would rather تعني «أفضّل» ويأتي بعدها الفعل الأصلي، وإذا جاء بعدها فاعل آخر نستخدم الماضي البسيط. وعبارة It's time مع الماضي البسيط تعني أن الوقت قد حان بل تأخر.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I wish I studied harder last year.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I wish I had studied harder last year.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الندم على الماضي يحتاج الماضي التام.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I wish I would have a car.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I wish I had a car.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نستخدم would مع المتكلم نفسه.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I'd rather to walk.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I'd rather walk.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا to بعد would rather.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It's time we go home.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It's time we went home.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد It's time + فاعل نستخدم الماضي.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I would rather you don't smoke here.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I would rather you didn't smoke here.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع فاعل آخر نستخدم الماضي.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>If only I can fly!</em> <strong>→ ✓ If only I could fly!</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">مع if only للحاضر نستخدم could.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Present wish: I wish I were at home. (I'm not at home now.)</p>\n<p>Past regret: I wish I had stayed at home. (I didn't stay.)</p>\n<p>Annoyance: I wish you would stay at home more. (You don't.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Time of the wish: now → past simple / were / could; past → past perfect.</p>\n<p>2. wish + would only for other people's behaviour or things.</p>\n<p>3. would rather + base verb; would rather + another subject + past simple.</p>\n<p>4. It's (high) time + subject + past simple.</p>\n<p>5. Look for time words (yesterday, last year) to choose the past perfect after wish.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد زمن الأمنية: الحاضر مع الماضي البسيط، والماضي مع الماضي التام، واستخدم wish + would لسلوك الآخرين فقط، وبعد would rather الفعل الأصلي، وبعد It's time + فاعل الماضي البسيط.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. I failed the test. I wish I ______ more time to revision.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. gave B. had given C. would give D. give</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The test is in the past — a regret.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Past regret → wish + past perfect.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">ندم على الماضي: had given.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. It's high time the government ______ more cycle lanes.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. build B. will build C. built D. has built</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> It's high time + subject.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The verb after it is past simple.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد It's high time + فاعل الماضي البسيط.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. I'd (A) <u>rather</u> (B) <u>to take</u> the (C) <u>metro</u> than (D) <u>drive</u> in this traffic.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. rather B. to take C. metro D. drive</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> would rather is followed by the base form.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> to take → take.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: I'd rather take the metro than drive in this traffic. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا to بعد would rather.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 D · 3 A · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 C · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I wish I ______ taller so I could play basketball better.","o":["am","were","will be","had been yesterday"],"k":1,"e":"Present wish → were.","h":"أمنية حاضرة were."},{"n":2,"s":"I wish I ______ to the party last night. Everyone says it was great.","o":["went","would go","had gone","go"],"k":2,"e":"Past regret → had gone.","h":"ندم على الماضي."},{"n":3,"s":"I wish my brother ______ borrowing my things without asking.","o":["stops","stopped already","had stop","would stop"],"k":3,"e":"Annoyance about another person → would stop.","h":"انزعاج من شخص آخر."},{"n":4,"s":"I'd rather ______ a book than watch TV.","o":["to read","reading","read","reads"],"k":2,"e":"would rather + base verb.","h":"would rather مع الفعل الأصلي."},{"n":5,"s":"It's time we ______ for the airport.","o":["left","leave","will leave","had left"],"k":0,"e":"It's time + subject + past simple.","h":"It's time مع الماضي."},{"n":6,"s":"If only I ______ his phone number! I could call him now.","o":["knew","know","would know","had know"],"k":0,"e":"Present wish → past simple.","h":"أمنية حاضرة."},{"n":7,"s":"She wishes she ______ the job offer last year.","o":["accepted","had accepted","would accept","accepts"],"k":1,"e":"Past regret → had accepted.","h":"ندم على الماضي."},{"n":8,"s":"My parents would rather I ______ at a university in Saudi Arabia.","o":["study","will study","studied","to study"],"k":2,"e":"would rather + another subject + past simple.","h":"مع فاعل آخر الماضي."},{"n":9,"s":"I wish it ______ raining. We want to go out.","o":["stops","would stop","stopped already","had stopped yesterday"],"k":1,"e":"Wanting a thing to change → would stop.","h":"رغبة في تغيير الحال."},{"n":10,"s":"It's high time you ______ seriously for the STEP.","o":["start studying","will start studying","had started study","started studying"],"k":3,"e":"It's high time + subject + past simple.","h":"It's high time مع الماضي."},{"n":11,"s":"If only I ______ that expensive phone. Now I have no money.","o":["hadn't bought","didn't buy","wouldn't buy","don't buy"],"k":0,"e":"Past regret → hadn't bought.","h":"ندم على الماضي."},{"n":12,"s":"Would you rather ______ by plane or by car?","o":["to travel","travelling","travel","travelled"],"k":2,"e":"would rather + base verb.","h":"would rather مع الفعل الأصلي."},{"n":13,"s":"I wish I ______ swim. My friends are all in the pool.","o":["can","could","would","had can"],"k":1,"e":"Present ability wish → could.","h":"أمنية بالقدرة could."},{"n":14,"s":"I'd rather you ______ your phone during dinner.","o":["don't use","won't use","not use","didn't use"],"k":3,"e":"would rather + another subject + past simple (negative).","h":"مع فاعل آخر الماضي."},{"n":15,"s":"He wishes he ______ so rude to his teacher yesterday.","o":["hadn't been","wasn't","wouldn't be","isn't"],"k":0,"e":"Past regret (yesterday) → hadn't been.","h":"ندم على الماضي."},{"n":16,"s":"It's about time the company ______ its workers a pay rise.","o":["give","gave","gives","will give"],"k":1,"e":"It's about time + subject + past simple.","h":"It's about time مع الماضي."},{"n":17,"s":"I wish people ______ so much plastic.","o":["wouldn't use","don't use","won't use","haven't used"],"k":0,"e":"Wanting others to change → wouldn't use.","h":"رغبة في تغيير سلوك الآخرين."},{"n":18,"s":"I'd rather stay here ______ go out in this heat.","o":["to","that","rather","than"],"k":3,"e":"would rather … than …","h":"would rather … than."},{"n":19,"s":"If only we ______ the map with us when we got lost!","o":["took","had taken","would take","take"],"k":1,"e":"Past regret → had taken.","h":"ندم على الماضي."},{"n":20,"s":"I wish I ______ more free time these days.","o":["have","would have","had","had had"],"k":2,"e":"Present wish (these days) → past simple had.","h":"أمنية حاضرة."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"I (A) wish I (B) studied (C) harder for the exam (D) last month.","o":["wish","studied","harder","last"],"k":1,"e":"Past regret → had studied.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"It's (A) almost midnight, so (B) it's time we (C) all (D) go home.","o":["almost","it's","all","go"],"k":3,"e":"It's time + subject + past simple.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"(A) I wish I would have a bigger room, but (B) our flat (C) is (D) small.","o":["I wish I would have","our","is","small"],"k":0,"e":"No would for yourself: I wish I had.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"My (A) father (B) would rather we (C) don't (D) travel at night.","o":["father","would rather","don't","travel"],"k":2,"e":"would rather + another subject + past simple.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"If (A) only I (B) can (C) remember his (D) name!","o":["only","can","remember","name"],"k":1,"e":"Present wish → could.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"I (A) wish my (B) neighbours (C) would stop (D) to make so much noise.","o":["wish","neighbours","would stop","to make"],"k":3,"e":"stop (= quit) + -ing: stop making.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"(A) She'd rather to stay at home than (B) go to (C) the (D) mall.","o":["She'd rather to stay","go","the","mall"],"k":0,"e":"would rather + base verb (no to).","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"If only we (A) had (B) not (C) sell our old house (D) last year!","o":["had","not","sell","last"],"k":2,"e":"had + past participle sold.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"It's (A) high time (B) the council (C) finally (D) repairs the roads.","o":["high","the","finally","repairs"],"k":3,"e":"It's high time + subject + past simple.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) I'd rather not to discuss (B) it (C) right (D) now.","o":["I'd rather not to","it","right","now"],"k":0,"e":"would rather (not) + base verb.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"4.5","t":"Advanced Passive, Causative have / get something done, Impersonal Passive","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.5 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Form the causative have / get something done in different tenses.</p>\n<p>2. Use impersonal passive structures (It is said that … / He is believed to …).</p>\n<p>3. Use passive infinitives and gerunds (to be done, being done).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يكوّن الطالب التركيب السببي have/get something done في أزمنة مختلفة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يستخدم تراكيب المبني للمجهول غير الشخصية مثل It is said that وHe is believed to.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم المصدر والاسم الفعلي في صيغة المبني للمجهول مثل to be done وbeing done.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. I ______ my hair cut every month.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. have B. make C. do D. let</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. It ______ that the new stadium will open next year.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. says B. is said C. has said D. said it</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Nobody likes ______ in front of the class.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. criticizing B. to criticize</p>\n<p>C. being criticized D. be criticized</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Causative have</strong></p>\n<p><strong>have + object + past participle (any tense)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We are having our kitchen painted. I had my phone repaired yesterday.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Causative get (less formal)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>get + object + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. You should get your eyes tested.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Impersonal passive (It …)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>It + is / was + said / believed / thought / reported / expected + that + clause</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. It is believed that the city was founded in 1300.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Personal passive (subject …)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subject + is / was + said / believed / thought + to + base verb / to have + p.p.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The city is believed to have been founded in 1300.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Passive infinitive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>to be + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The report needs to be finished by Monday.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Passive gerund</strong></p>\n<p><strong>being + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She hates being interrupted.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Passive with modals (perfect)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>should / must / could + have been + p.p.</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The problem should have been solved earlier.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Causative: someone else does a service for us.</strong></p>\n<p>We do not do the action ourselves; we arrange for another person to do it.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My father had the car washed at the petrol station.</p>\n<p>▸ I'm going to get my laptop fixed tomorrow.</p>\n<p>▸ Have you had your passport renewed yet?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Causative for bad experiences.</strong></p>\n<p>have something done can also describe something bad that happened to us.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ He had his wallet stolen on the metro.</p>\n<p>▸ We had our windows broken during the storm.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Impersonal passive: reporting general beliefs and news.</strong></p>\n<p>This structure is common in academic and news texts — and in STEP reading.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ It is said that the old castle is haunted.</p>\n<p>▸ It is expected that prices will rise.</p>\n<p>▸ The suspect is thought to be hiding in the mountains.</p>\n<p>▸ Ibn Battuta is known to have travelled about 120,000 km.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Passive infinitives and gerunds.</strong></p>\n<p>After verbs that need to or -ing, the passive form uses to be done or being done.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The windows need to be cleaned.</p>\n<p>▸ I don't like being told what to do.</p>\n<p>▸ The results are expected to be announced tonight.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Word order in the causative: have + OBJECT + p.p. — ✗ I had cut my hair (= I cut it myself, earlier). ✓ I had my hair cut.</p>\n<p>▸ Use to have + p.p. in personal passive for an earlier action: He is said to have left the country.</p>\n<p>▸ need + -ing can also have passive meaning: The car needs washing. (= needs to be washed)</p>\n<p>▸ Choose the correct tense of have in causatives: is having, had, will have, has had.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">التركيب السببي have أو get مع المفعول ثم التصريف الثالث يعني أننا جعلنا شخصًا آخر يقوم بالعمل لنا، مثل I had my car washed، ويتغير زمن have حسب الجملة.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المبني للمجهول غير الشخصي يُستخدم كثيرًا في الأخبار والنصوص الأكاديمية: It is said that + جملة، أو الفاعل + is said + to + الفعل، وإذا كان الحدث سابقًا نستخدم to have + التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد الأفعال التي يأتي بعدها to نستخدم to be + التصريف الثالث، وبعد الأفعال وحروف الجر التي يأتي بعدها ing نستخدم being + التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I cut my hair at the barber's.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I had my hair cut at the barber's.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الحلاق قص الشعر فنستخدم التركيب السببي.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I had repaired my car yesterday. (by a mechanic)</em> <strong>→ ✓ I had my car repaired yesterday.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المفعول يأتي قبل التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It is said the city to be old.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It is said that the city is old. / The city is said to be old.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نخلط بين التركيبين.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The report needs to finish today.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The report needs to be finished today.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">التقرير يقع عليه الحدث فنستخدم to be finished.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She doesn't like to being criticized.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She doesn't like being criticized.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المبني للمجهول من ing هو being + p.p.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He is believed to leave the country last year.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He is believed to have left the country last year.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للحدث السابق نستخدم to have + p.p.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Active: The mechanic repaired my car.</p>\n<p>Passive: My car was repaired (by the mechanic).</p>\n<p>Causative: I had / got my car repaired.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. If someone else does the job for the subject → have / get + object + p.p.</p>\n<p>2. It is said / believed + that + clause; Subject + is said / believed + to + verb.</p>\n<p>3. Earlier action in a personal passive → to have + p.p.</p>\n<p>4. After need / want / expect + to → to be + p.p.; after enjoy / hate / avoid / prepositions → being + p.p.</p>\n<p>5. STEP traps: wrong word order (had repaired my car), missing be, -ing vs p.p.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذا قام شخص آخر بالعمل لصالح الفاعل فاستخدم have/get + المفعول + التصريف الثالث، وفي التراكيب غير الشخصية انتبه للفرق بين that وto، وللحدث السابق استخدم to have + p.p.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. We ______ by a professional photographer at my sister's graduation.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. took our photos B. had our photos taken</p>\n<p>C. had taken our photos D. were taking photos</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Someone else (the photographer) did the action for us.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Causative: have + object + p.p.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المصور قام بالعمل لنا: had our photos taken.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The pyramids are believed ______ more than 4,500 years ago.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. to build B. to be built</p>\n<p>C. to have been built D. being built</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Personal passive: Subject + is believed + to …</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> The building happened earlier and the pyramids received the action.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> to have been + p.p. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدث سابق مبني للمجهول: to have been built.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. All the (A) <u>forms</u> need (B) <u>to</u> (C) <u>fill</u> in before (D) <u>the</u> interview.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. forms B. to C. fill D. the</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The forms do not fill themselves — passive meaning.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> need + to be + p.p.: to be filled.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: All the forms need to be filled in before the interview. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المبني للمجهول بعد need: to be filled.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 A · 2 B · 3 C · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 C · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"I need to ______ my eyes tested before I renew my licence.","o":["make","do","let","have"],"k":3,"e":"Causative: have + object + p.p.","h":"التركيب السببي have."},{"n":2,"s":"My mother is ______ the kitchen redesigned this month.","o":["doing","making","having","letting"],"k":2,"e":"Present continuous causative: is having + object + p.p.","h":"السببي في المستمر."},{"n":3,"s":"We had our carpets ______ before the guests arrived.","o":["clean","cleaned","cleaning","to clean"],"k":1,"e":"have + object + past participle.","h":"المفعول ثم التصريف الثالث."},{"n":4,"s":"It ______ that the meeting will be postponed.","o":["expects","is expected","is expecting","has expected"],"k":1,"e":"Impersonal passive: It is expected that …","h":"المبني للمجهول غير الشخصي."},{"n":5,"s":"He is said ______ the richest man in the town.","o":["to be","being","that he is","be"],"k":0,"e":"Subject + is said + to + verb.","h":"is said + to."},{"n":6,"s":"The new bridge needs ______ before the rainy season.","o":["to repair","to be repaired","repairing it","be repaired"],"k":1,"e":"Passive infinitive: to be + p.p.","h":"to be + p.p."},{"n":7,"s":"My little brother hates ______ a baby.","o":["to call","calling","be called","being called"],"k":3,"e":"hate + -ing; passive meaning → being called.","h":"being + p.p."},{"n":8,"s":"I got my phone ______ at a small shop near the souq.","o":["fix","fixing","fixed","to fix"],"k":2,"e":"get + object + p.p.","h":"get + المفعول + p.p."},{"n":9,"s":"It is believed ______ the old tower was built by a local king.","o":["that","to","what","being"],"k":0,"e":"It is believed + that + clause.","h":"It is believed that."},{"n":10,"s":"The singer is thought ______ the country last week.","o":["to leave","to have left","leaving","that left"],"k":1,"e":"Earlier action → to have + p.p.","h":"حدث سابق to have + p.p."},{"n":11,"s":"Ahmed ______ his bike stolen outside the library.","o":["made","did","got to","had"],"k":3,"e":"Bad experience causative: had + object + p.p.","h":"تجربة سيئة had."},{"n":12,"s":"These letters must ______ before 5 p.m.","o":["post","posted","be posted","be posting"],"k":2,"e":"Modal passive: must be + p.p.","h":"must be + p.p."},{"n":13,"s":"The suspect is reported ______ in a hotel near the border.","o":["hiding","to hide yesterday","to be hiding","that he hides"],"k":2,"e":"Personal passive, action in progress now → to be + -ing.","h":"حدث مستمر to be + ing."},{"n":14,"s":"Have you ______ your hair cut? It looks great!","o":["made","done","let","had"],"k":3,"e":"Present perfect causative: have had + object + p.p.","h":"السببي في التام."},{"n":15,"s":"Nobody enjoys ______ at by strangers in the street.","o":["being shouted","shouting","to be shouted","be shouted"],"k":0,"e":"enjoy + -ing; passive → being shouted.","h":"being + p.p."},{"n":16,"s":"It was reported that three people ______ in the accident.","o":["had injured","were injuring","had been injured","injured themselves by"],"k":2,"e":"Past perfect passive in a report.","h":"الماضي التام المبني للمجهول."},{"n":17,"s":"This problem should ______ years ago.","o":["have solved","be solved","have been solved","solved"],"k":2,"e":"Past modal passive: should have been + p.p.","h":"should have been + p.p."},{"n":18,"s":"We're going to have a new air conditioner ______ next week.","o":["installed","install","installing","to install"],"k":0,"e":"have + object + p.p.","h":"التصريف الثالث installed."},{"n":19,"s":"Ibn Sina is known ______ more than 400 works.","o":["to write","writing","that wrote","to have written"],"k":3,"e":"Earlier action → to have + p.p.","h":"حدث سابق."},{"n":20,"s":"The students expect ______ the results by email.","o":["to send","to be sent","sending","be sent"],"k":1,"e":"The students receive the action → passive infinitive.","h":"الطلاب يقع عليهم الحدث."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"I (A) cut my hair (B) at (C) the barber's (D) yesterday.","o":["cut","at","the","yesterday"],"k":0,"e":"The barber did it → causative had … cut.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"We (A) had (B) painted our (C) house (D) last month by a company.","o":["had","painted","house","last"],"k":1,"e":"Word order: had + object + p.p.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"The (A) new museum (B) is expected (C) to (D) open by the minister next month.","o":["new","is expected","to","open"],"k":3,"e":"The museum receives the action → to be opened.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"The (A) report needs (B) to (C) finish (D) by Thursday.","o":["report","to","finish","by"],"k":2,"e":"Passive infinitive: to be finished.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) She hates to being told what to wear by (B) her (C) older (D) sisters.","o":["She hates to being","her","older","sisters"],"k":0,"e":"like + being + p.p.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"He (A) is (B) believed (C) by many people (D) to leave the country last year.","o":["is","believed","by","to leave"],"k":3,"e":"Earlier action → to have left.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"The (A) missing boat (B) is thought (C) that (D) it sank near the island.","o":["missing","is","that","it sank"],"k":2,"e":"Subject + is thought + to …","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"Did you (A) get (B) renew your passport (C) in (D) time?","o":["get","renew","in","time"],"k":1,"e":"get + object + p.p. (renewed after the object).","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"These (A) old documents (B) must (C) be (D) keep safely.","o":["old","must","be","keep"],"k":3,"e":"Modal passive: must be + past participle kept.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"We (A) are repairing the roof (B) this week; a (C) company (D) is doing the work.","o":["are repairing","this","company","is"],"k":0,"e":"A company does the job → causative are having … repaired.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"4.6","t":"Reporting Verbs and Their Patterns","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.6 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use reporting verbs with the right pattern (advise sb to, deny -ing, suggest -ing / that).</p>\n<p>2. Choose a reporting verb that matches the speaker's function (warn, admit, insist, refuse, apologize).</p>\n<p>3. Detect pattern errors such as suggested him to go.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب أفعال النقل مع النمط الصحيح بعد كل فعل.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختار فعل النقل الذي يطابق وظيفة كلام المتكلم مثل warn وadmit وinsist وrefuse وapologize.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يكتشف أخطاء الأنماط مثل suggested him to go.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. He admitted ______ the window.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. to break B. breaking C. that break D. break</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. The doctor advised me ______ more water.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. drink B. drinking C. to drink D. that drink</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. She suggested ______ to the beach.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. going B. to go C. us to go D. go</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>verb + to-infinitive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>agree · refuse · promise · offer · threaten · decide · claim</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He refused to answer. She promised to call.</em></p>\n<p><strong>verb + object + to-infinitive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>advise · tell · ask · warn · remind · encourage · persuade · invite · order</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The teacher reminded us to bring our books.</em></p>\n<p><strong>verb + -ing</strong></p>\n<p><strong>deny · admit · suggest · recommend · mention · regret</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He denied taking the money. She suggested leaving early.</em></p>\n<p><strong>verb + preposition + -ing</strong></p>\n<p><strong>apologize for · insist on · accuse sb of · blame sb for · congratulate sb on · thank sb for</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He apologized for being late. They accused him of cheating.</em></p>\n<p><strong>verb + that-clause</strong></p>\n<p><strong>explain · admit · suggest · insist · agree · announce · complain · claim</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She suggested that we (should) take a taxi.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Negatives</strong></p>\n<p><strong>verb + object + not to · verb + not + -ing</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He warned me not to touch it. She regretted not studying.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Reporting verbs summarize the function of what was said.</strong></p>\n<p>Instead of said, we choose a verb that shows the speaker's purpose.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ \"I'll help you.\" → He offered to help me.</p>\n<p>▸ \"I didn't take it.\" → She denied taking it.</p>\n<p>▸ \"You should rest.\" → The doctor advised me to rest.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Verbs with an object + to-infinitive.</strong></p>\n<p>These verbs need a person before to.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ My father encouraged me to apply for the scholarship.</p>\n<p>▸ The guide warned the tourists not to swim there.</p>\n<p>▸ She persuaded her brother to join the club.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Verbs with -ing or a preposition + -ing.</strong></p>\n<p>These verbs never take to.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ He admitted forgetting the tickets.</p>\n<p>▸ The coach insisted on training every day.</p>\n<p>▸ We congratulated Huda on winning the competition.</p>\n<p>▸ They blamed the driver for causing the accident.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. suggest and recommend.</strong></p>\n<p>suggest / recommend + -ing or + that + subject + (should) + base verb — never + object + to.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I suggest leaving now.</p>\n<p>▸ The teacher suggested that we read the article again.</p>\n<p>▸ Doctors recommend drinking eight glasses of water a day.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ ✗ He suggested me to go. ✓ He suggested (that) I go / should go. ✓ He suggested going.</p>\n<p>▸ explain + to + person: She explained the rule to us. (not explained us)</p>\n<p>▸ deny / admit + -ing or + having + p.p. for a past action: He denied having seen her.</p>\n<p>▸ say and tell are not followed by to-infinitive with the meaning of advise: ✓ He told me to wait.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">أفعال النقل تلخّص وظيفة الكلام بدل said، ولكل فعل نمط خاص يجب حفظه: بعض الأفعال يأتي بعدها to مثل agree وrefuse وpromise، وبعضها يحتاج مفعولًا ثم to مثل advise وwarn وremind.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">وهناك أفعال يأتي بعدها الفعل بـ ing مثل deny وadmit وsuggest، وأفعال يأتي بعدها حرف جر ثم ing مثل apologize for وinsist on وaccuse someone of.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الفعل suggest لا يأتي بعده مفعول ثم to، فلا نقول suggested me to go، بل suggested going أو suggested that I go.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He suggested me to see a doctor.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He suggested that I see a doctor. / He suggested seeing a doctor.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">suggest لا يأتي بعدها مفعول + to.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She denied to take the money.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She denied taking the money.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">deny مع ing.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He apologized to be late.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He apologized for being late.</strong></p>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">apologize for + ing.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>They insisted to pay.</em> <strong>→ ✓ They insisted on paying.</strong></p>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">insist on + ing.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The teacher explained us the rule.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The teacher explained the rule to us.</strong></p>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">explain something to someone.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He warned me don't touch it.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He warned me not to touch it.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">النهي مع warn: not to.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>promise to: He promised to come.</p>\n<p>remind sb to: He reminded me to come.</p>\n<p>insist on -ing: He insisted on coming. · suggest -ing: He suggested coming.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Identify the reporting verb, then recall its pattern (to / object + to / -ing / preposition + -ing / that).</p>\n<p>2. Check for a missing or extra object (suggested me ✗, warned not to ✗ without a person).</p>\n<p>3. Prepositions are fixed: accuse of, blame for, apologize for, insist on, congratulate on.</p>\n<p>4. Match meaning: an offer → offer; denying → deny; admitting → admit; strong demand → insist.</p>\n<p>5. STEP error items love suggest + object + to and deny + to.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">حدّد فعل النقل ثم تذكّر نمطه: to أم مفعول + to أم ing أم حرف جر + ing أم that، وانتبه لحروف الجر الثابتة ولخطأ suggest + مفعول + to.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The manager accused the employee ______ the report.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. to lose B. of losing C. for losing D. losing</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The reporting verb is accuse.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Pattern: accuse somebody of + -ing.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">accuse someone of + ing.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. My uncle ______ to drive me to the airport.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. suggested B. offered C. insisted D. denied</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The blank is followed by to + verb.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Of the options, only offer takes to-infinitive with this meaning.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">offer يأتي بعده to.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. The (A) <u>coach</u> (B) <u>suggested</u> (C) <u>us to train</u> (D) <u>harder</u> before the final.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. coach B. suggested C. us to train D. harder</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> suggest cannot take object + to.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> suggested us to train → suggested that we train / suggested training.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: The coach suggested that we train harder before the final. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">suggest لا يأتي بعدها مفعول + to.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 C · 3 A · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"She promised ______ me with my project.","o":["helping","to help","me to help","that help"],"k":1,"e":"promise + to-infinitive.","h":"promise مع to."},{"n":2,"s":"The doctor advised my father ______ smoking.","o":["stopping","stop","that stop","to stop"],"k":3,"e":"advise + object + to.","h":"advise + مفعول + to."},{"n":3,"s":"He denied ______ the money.","o":["taking","to take","take","that take"],"k":0,"e":"deny + -ing.","h":"deny مع ing."},{"n":4,"s":"The student apologized ______ late.","o":["to be","being for","for being","of being"],"k":2,"e":"apologize for + -ing.","h":"apologize for + ing."},{"n":5,"s":"My friend suggested ______ to the new restaurant.","o":["going","to go","us to go","go"],"k":0,"e":"suggest + -ing.","h":"suggest مع ing."},{"n":6,"s":"The teacher reminded us ______ our homework.","o":["bringing","bring","for bringing","to bring"],"k":3,"e":"remind + object + to.","h":"remind + مفعول + to."},{"n":7,"s":"He refused ______ the question.","o":["answering","answer","to answer","for answering"],"k":2,"e":"refuse + to.","h":"refuse مع to."},{"n":8,"s":"They congratulated me ______ my exams.","o":["for pass","on passing","to pass","of passing"],"k":1,"e":"congratulate somebody on + -ing.","h":"congratulate on + ing."},{"n":9,"s":"The guide warned us ______ near the edge.","o":["don't go","not to go","not going","to not going"],"k":1,"e":"warn + object + not to.","h":"warn + مفعول + not to."},{"n":10,"s":"She admitted ______ the last piece of cake.","o":["eating","to eat","eat","for eating"],"k":0,"e":"admit + -ing.","h":"admit مع ing."},{"n":11,"s":"My parents encouraged me ______ for the scholarship.","o":["applying","apply","to apply","for applying"],"k":2,"e":"encourage + object + to.","h":"encourage + مفعول + to."},{"n":12,"s":"The players insisted ______ in the rain.","o":["to play","playing","for playing","on playing"],"k":3,"e":"insist on + -ing.","h":"insist on + ing."},{"n":13,"s":"He ______ that he had never seen the man before.","o":["suggested us","warned","claimed","told"],"k":2,"e":"claim + that-clause (no object).","h":"claim + that."},{"n":14,"s":"The police accused him ______ the car.","o":["of stealing","for stealing","to steal","stealing"],"k":0,"e":"accuse somebody of + -ing.","h":"accuse of + ing."},{"n":15,"s":"\"Shall I carry your bag?\" → He ______ to carry my bag.","o":["suggested","insisted","offered","admitted"],"k":2,"e":"An offer → offered + to.","h":"عرض offered."},{"n":16,"s":"The teacher explained ______ how to solve the problem.","o":["us","to us","for us","at us"],"k":1,"e":"explain + to + person.","h":"explain to + شخص."},{"n":17,"s":"She persuaded her brother ______ the swimming team.","o":["joining","to join","join","for joining"],"k":1,"e":"persuade + object + to.","h":"persuade + مفعول + to."},{"n":18,"s":"The company blamed the weather ______ the delay.","o":["of","on","to","for"],"k":3,"e":"blame something for something.","h":"blame for."},{"n":19,"s":"Experts recommend ______ at least seven hours a night.","o":["to sleep","us to sleep","sleeping","sleep"],"k":2,"e":"recommend + -ing.","h":"recommend مع ing."},{"n":20,"s":"\"I'm sorry, but I won't lend you my car.\" → She ______ to lend me her car.","o":["refused","denied","suggested","apologized"],"k":0,"e":"Saying no to a request → refused + to.","h":"الرفض refused."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"He (A) suggested (B) me (C) to visit the (D) museum.","o":["suggested","me","to visit","museum"],"k":2,"e":"suggest cannot take object + to.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"(A) She denied to break the vase, but (B) her brother (C) saw (D) her.","o":["She denied to break","her","saw","her"],"k":0,"e":"deny + -ing.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"The (A) students (B) apologized (C) to their teacher (D) to be late.","o":["students","apologized","to their teacher","to be"],"k":3,"e":"apologize for + -ing.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"My (A) father (B) insisted to pay for (C) everyone's (D) dinner.","o":["father","insisted to pay","everyone's","dinner"],"k":1,"e":"insist on + -ing.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"The (A) guide (B) warned the (C) tourists (D) don't swim near the rocks.","o":["guide","warned","tourists","don't swim"],"k":3,"e":"warn + object + not to.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"(A) The teacher (B) explained (C) us the (D) new rule.","o":["The","explained","us","new"],"k":2,"e":"explain something to someone.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"(A) They accused him for cheating (B) in (C) the (D) exam.","o":["They accused him for","in","the","exam"],"k":0,"e":"accuse somebody of + -ing.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"He (A) promised (B) calling me (C) as soon as he (D) arrived.","o":["promised","calling","as soon as","arrived"],"k":1,"e":"promise + to.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"The (A) coach (B) encouraged the (C) players (D) train harder.","o":["coach","encouraged","players","train"],"k":3,"e":"encourage + object + to.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"(A) She admitted to forget my birthday and (B) said (C) she was (D) sorry.","o":["She admitted to forget","said","she","sorry"],"k":0,"e":"admit + -ing.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"4.7","t":"Past Modals: must have, can't have, should have, needn't have","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.7 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Make deductions about the past with must have / can't have / might have / could have + past participle.</p>\n<p>2. Express criticism and regret with should have / shouldn't have / ought to have.</p>\n<p>3. Tell needn't have done (did it, but it was not necessary) from didn't need to do (not necessary, so probably not done).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستنتج الطالب أمورًا في الماضي باستخدام must have وcan't have وmight have وcould have مع التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يعبّر عن اللوم والندم باستخدام should have وshouldn't have.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يميّز بين needn't have done وdidn't need to do.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. The ground is wet. It ______ during the night.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. must rain B. must have rained</p>\n<p>C. can't have rained D. should rain</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. You failed because you didn't study. You ______ harder.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. should have studied B. must have studied</p>\n<p>C. can't have studied D. needn't study</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. He ______ the email. He wasn't at work yesterday.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. must have sent B. should have sent</p>\n<p>C. can't have sent D. needn't have sent</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Deduction: almost certain YES</strong></p>\n<p><strong>must have + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She must have left early. Her car isn't here.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Deduction: almost certain NO</strong></p>\n<p><strong>can't have / couldn't have + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He can't have seen us. It was too dark.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Possibility</strong></p>\n<p><strong>might / may / could have + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. They might have taken the wrong road.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Criticism / regret</strong></p>\n<p><strong>should have / shouldn't have / ought to have + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. You should have told me. I shouldn't have eaten so much.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Unnecessary action that happened</strong></p>\n<p><strong>needn't have + past participle</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. We needn't have brought food; there was plenty.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Not necessary (usually not done)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>didn't need to / didn't have to + base verb</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. I didn't need to wake up early, so I slept until nine.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Continuous</strong></p>\n<p><strong>must / might / can't have been + -ing</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. She must have been sleeping when you called.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Deductions about the past.</strong></p>\n<p>We use the evidence we have now to guess what happened.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ The streets are white. It must have snowed in Tabuk last night.</p>\n<p>▸ Ali can't have written this — it's not his handwriting.</p>\n<p>▸ I can't find my keys. I might have left them in the car.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Criticism and regret.</strong></p>\n<p>should have = it was the right thing, but it didn't happen; shouldn't have = it happened, but it was wrong.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ You should have checked the map before the trip.</p>\n<p>▸ I shouldn't have shouted at my brother.</p>\n<p>▸ The government ought to have built the bridge years ago.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. needn't have vs didn't need to.</strong></p>\n<p>needn't have done = you did it, but it was unnecessary; didn't need to = it was not necessary (we often don't know if you did it).</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ I needn't have bought milk — we already had two bottles.</p>\n<p>▸ We didn't need to show our tickets, so we just walked in.</p>\n<p>▸ You needn't have cooked so much food!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. could have: a past possibility that didn't happen.</strong></p>\n<p>could have also shows that something was possible but did not happen.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ You could have hurt yourself! Be careful.</p>\n<p>▸ We could have won the match if we had played better.</p>\n<p>▸ She could have become a doctor, but she chose engineering.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Always have + PAST PARTICIPLE after the modal: ✗ must have went ✓ must have gone.</p>\n<p>▸ mustn't have is NOT used for negative deduction: ✓ can't have.</p>\n<p>▸ Pronunciation: should've, must've, might've — never should of.</p>\n<p>▸ These forms are very common in STEP items with evidence clues (because, so, but).</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للاستنتاج في الماضي نستخدم الفعل الناقص ثم have ثم التصريف الثالث: must have للتأكيد، وcan't have للنفي القوي، وmight have أو could have للاحتمال.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للتعبير عن اللوم أو الندم نستخدم should have (كان ينبغي أن… ولم يحدث)، وshouldn't have (ما كان ينبغي… وقد حدث).</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">needn't have done تعني أن الفعل حدث لكنه لم يكن ضروريًا، أما didn't need to فتعني أنه لم يكن ضروريًا، والغالب أنه لم يحدث.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>She must have went home.</em> <strong>→ ✓ She must have gone home.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد have التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He mustn't have seen me.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He can't have seen me.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الاستنتاج المنفي can't have.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>You should have tell me.</em> <strong>→ ✓ You should have told me.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">should have + التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>I needn't have to bring food.</em> <strong>→ ✓ I needn't have brought food.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">needn't have + التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>You should of called.</em> <strong>→ ✓ You should have called.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">should've تُكتب should have.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>It must rain last night.</em> <strong>→ ✓ It must have rained last night.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للماضي must have + p.p.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Present deduction: He must be tired. (now)</p>\n<p>Past deduction: He must have been tired. (then)</p>\n<p>Criticism: He should have rested. / He shouldn't have worked so late.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. Is the sentence about the past? Then modal + have + past participle.</p>\n<p>2. Evidence for yes → must have; for no → can't have; unsure → might / could have.</p>\n<p>3. Criticism or regret → should / shouldn't have.</p>\n<p>4. needn't have = done but unnecessary; didn't need to = not necessary.</p>\n<p>5. Check the participle (gone, seen, taken, written).</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">إذا كان الحديث عن الماضي فاستخدم الفعل الناقص + have + التصريف الثالث، واختر must have للتأكيد وcan't have للنفي وshould have للوم، وانتبه للفرق بين needn't have وdidn't need to.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. Sami got 100% in the test. He ______ very hard.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. must have studied B. should have studied</p>\n<p>C. can't have studied D. needn't have studied</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The evidence (100%) is strong.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Past deduction, yes → must have + p.p.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is A.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">استنتاج مؤكد في الماضي: must have studied.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. We ______ an umbrella. It didn't rain at all.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. can't have taken B. needn't have taken</p>\n<p>C. must have taken D. didn't need take</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> We took an umbrella, but it was not necessary.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Done but unnecessary → needn't have + p.p.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">فعلناه ولم يكن ضروريًا: needn't have taken.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. You (A) <u>should have</u> (B) <u>telled</u> me that you (C) <u>were</u> (D) <u>coming</u>.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. should have B. telled C. were D. coming</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> should have needs a past participle.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> tell → told.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: You should have told me that you were coming. The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">should have + told.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 A · 3 C · Worked examples: Example 1 A · Example 2 B · Example 3 B","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"The window is broken. Someone ______ it with a ball.","o":["must have hit","must hit","can't have hit","should hit"],"k":0,"e":"Strong evidence → must have + p.p.","h":"استنتاج مؤكد."},{"n":2,"s":"He ______ the message. His phone was switched off all day.","o":["can't have received","must have received","should have received","needn't receive"],"k":0,"e":"Strong evidence for no → can't have.","h":"استنتاج منفي."},{"n":3,"s":"You ______ me you were ill. I would have visited you.","o":["must have told","can't have told","should have told","should tell"],"k":2,"e":"Criticism → should have + p.p.","h":"لوم should have."},{"n":4,"s":"I'm not sure where she is. She ______ to the library.","o":["must go","might have gone","should have gone","can't go"],"k":1,"e":"Possibility → might have + p.p.","h":"احتمال might have."},{"n":5,"s":"I feel sick. I ______ so many sweets.","o":["mustn't have eaten","shouldn't have eaten","can't have eaten","needn't eat"],"k":1,"e":"Regret → shouldn't have.","h":"ندم shouldn't have."},{"n":6,"s":"We ______ so early. The shop didn't open until ten.","o":["needn't have arrived","didn't need arrive","mustn't have arrived","can't have arrived"],"k":0,"e":"Done but unnecessary → needn't have.","h":"فعلناه دون حاجة."},{"n":7,"s":"The road is wet. It ______ while we were inside.","o":["must rain","should have rained","must have rained","needn't rain"],"k":2,"e":"Past deduction → must have rained.","h":"استنتاج مؤكد."},{"n":8,"s":"Huda ______ the answer. She has never studied this topic.","o":["must have known","should have known","needn't know","can't have known"],"k":3,"e":"Impossible → can't have known.","h":"مستحيل."},{"n":9,"s":"You ______ yourself! Don't climb on that wall again.","o":["must have hurt","should hurt","can't hurt","could have hurt"],"k":3,"e":"A past danger that didn't happen → could have.","h":"خطر لم يحدث could have."},{"n":10,"s":"They ______ the wrong turn; that's why they're late.","o":["must have took","must have taken","should taken","can't took"],"k":1,"e":"must have + taken.","h":"التصريف الثالث taken."},{"n":11,"s":"It was a public holiday, so I ______ go to work.","o":["needn't have","mustn't","didn't need to","can't have"],"k":2,"e":"Not necessary (and not done) → didn't need to.","h":"لم يكن ضروريًا."},{"n":12,"s":"The team ______ more. They lost because they were unfit.","o":["must have trained","should have trained","can't have trained","should train"],"k":1,"e":"Criticism about the past → should have.","h":"لوم على الماضي."},{"n":13,"s":"I can't find my wallet. I ______ it on the bus.","o":["may have left","must leave","should have left","need have left"],"k":0,"e":"Possibility → may have + p.p.","h":"احتمال."},{"n":14,"s":"She looks very tired. She ______ well last night.","o":["mustn't have slept","should sleep","needn't have slept","can't have slept"],"k":3,"e":"Negative deduction → can't have.","h":"استنتاج منفي."},{"n":15,"s":"You ______ all that food. Only three guests came.","o":["didn't need cook","needn't have cooked","mustn't have cooked","can't have cooked"],"k":1,"e":"Done but unnecessary → needn't have.","h":"فعلتِه دون حاجة."},{"n":16,"s":"He wasn't answering. He ______ in a meeting.","o":["must be been","should have been","must have been","can't be"],"k":2,"e":"Past deduction with be → must have been.","h":"استنتاج ماضٍ مع be."},{"n":17,"s":"Faisal ______ the bus. He usually arrives at eight, and it's already nine.","o":["should miss","can't miss","needn't have missed","might have missed"],"k":3,"e":"A possible explanation → might have missed.","h":"تفسير محتمل."},{"n":18,"s":"They ______ the house before they bought it. Now they've found many problems.","o":["must have inspected","needn't have inspected","can't have inspected","should have inspected"],"k":3,"e":"Criticism → should have.","h":"لوم."},{"n":19,"s":"When I got home, the lights were off. My family ______ to bed.","o":["must have went","should have gone","must have gone","needn't go"],"k":2,"e":"Past deduction → must have gone.","h":"استنتاج مؤكد."},{"n":20,"s":"The driver ______ the red light. That's why the police stopped him.","o":["must have ignored","can't have ignored","needn't have ignored","should ignore"],"k":0,"e":"Strong evidence → must have ignored.","h":"دليل قوي."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"(A) She must have (B) forget (C) her keys; the door (D) is still locked.","o":["She","forget","her","is"],"k":1,"e":"must have + forgotten.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"He (A) mustn't have (B) seen us; (C) he was looking (D) the other way.","o":["mustn't have","seen","he","the other way"],"k":0,"e":"Negative deduction → can't have.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"You (A) should (B) have (C) to call the doctor (D) earlier.","o":["should","have","to call","earlier"],"k":2,"e":"should have + past participle.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"We (A) needn't have (B) bought (C) a new printer; the old one (D) was worked fine.","o":["needn't have","bought","a","was worked"],"k":3,"e":"Active past simple worked.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"It (A) must (B) rain last night; the (C) streets are (D) wet.","o":["must","rain","streets","wet"],"k":1,"e":"Past deduction → must have rained.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"I (A) shouldn't (B) have (C) stay up so (D) late.","o":["shouldn't","have","stay","late"],"k":2,"e":"shouldn't have + stayed.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"(A) He might (B) had (C) taken the (D) wrong train.","o":["He might","had","taken","wrong"],"k":1,"e":"might have, not might had.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"You (A) could have (B) been (C) hurt! You (D) should to wear a helmet.","o":["could have","been","hurt","should to wear"],"k":3,"e":"No to after should.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) They should of (B) booked the tickets (C) earlier; now (D) it's sold out.","o":["They should of","booked","earlier","it's"],"k":0,"e":"should have (not should of).","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"The exam (A) was cancelled, so we (B) didn't (C) need (D) studying.","o":["was","didn't","need","studying"],"k":3,"e":"didn't need + to-infinitive.","h":""}]}],"n":30},{"id":"4.8","t":"Advanced Relative Clauses and Participle Clauses","html":"<p><strong>Unit 4 · Lesson 4.8 · CEFR B2 · STEP link: Sentence Structure (completion + error identification)</strong></p>\n<h3>Objectives</h3>\n<p>1. Use prepositions with relative pronouns (in which, to whom, most of which, some of whom).</p>\n<p>2. Reduce relative clauses to participle clauses (-ing / -ed).</p>\n<p>3. Use participle clauses for time and reason and avoid dangling participles.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">الأهداف</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">١. أن يستخدم الطالب حروف الجر مع ضمائر الوصل مثل in which وto whom وmost of which.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٢. أن يختصر جمل الصلة إلى جمل فعلية بصيغة ing أو التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">٣. أن يستخدم جمل اسم الفاعل والمفعول للزمن والسبب ويتجنب أخطاء الفاعل المعلّق.</span></p>\n<h3>Warm-up (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>1. The house ______ I grew up has been sold.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. which B. in which C. whom D. who</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. The man ______ next to me on the plane was a doctor.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. sitting B. sat C. sits D. was sitting</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. ______ by a famous architect, the museum attracts many visitors.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Designing B. Designs C. It designed D. Designed</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Form</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Preposition + which / whom (formal)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>noun + preposition + which (things) / whom (people) + clause</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. the city in which I was born · the person to whom I spoke</em></p>\n<p><strong>Quantifier + of + which / whom</strong></p>\n<p><strong>some / many / most / all / none / both + of + which / whom</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. He has three brothers, all of whom are engineers.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Reduced relative: active</strong></p>\n<p><strong>noun + verb-ing (= who / which + active verb)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The girl talking to Huda is my cousin. (= who is talking)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Reduced relative: passive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>noun + past participle (= who / which + passive verb)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. The cars made in this factory are exported. (= which are made)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Participle clause: time / reason (active)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>-ing …, main clause (same subject)</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Feeling tired, I went to bed early. (= Because I felt tired)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Participle clause: earlier action</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Having + p.p. …, main clause</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Having finished the exam, the students left the hall.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Participle clause: passive</strong></p>\n<p><strong>p.p. …, main clause</strong></p>\n<p><em>e.g. Built in 1865, the fortress is now a museum.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Use</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Formal relative clauses with prepositions.</strong></p>\n<p>In formal writing, the preposition comes before which / whom.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ This is the research on which the report is based.</p>\n<p>▸ The teacher to whom you should give the form is in Room 4.</p>\n<p>▸ The village, in which my father was born, is near Abha.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>2. Quantity + of which / of whom.</strong></p>\n<p>We use them in non-defining clauses to give information about part of a group.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ We visited ten cities, most of which were very modern.</p>\n<p>▸ She has two sisters, both of whom live in Jeddah.</p>\n<p>▸ The class has thirty students, none of whom failed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>3. Reduced relative clauses.</strong></p>\n<p>We can make relative clauses shorter with -ing (active) or a past participle (passive).</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ People living in Riyadh are used to the heat.</p>\n<p>▸ The questions asked in the interview were difficult.</p>\n<p>▸ Anyone wanting to join the trip should sign up today.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>4. Participle clauses at the start of a sentence.</strong></p>\n<p>The subject of the participle must be the same as the subject of the main clause.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>▸ Walking along the Corniche, we saw dolphins in the sea.</p>\n<p>▸ Having lived in Canada for years, Majed speaks English fluently.</p>\n<p>▸ Surrounded by mountains, Abha has a cool climate.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Signal Words and Notes</h3>\n<p>▸ Dangling participle: ✗ Walking to school, the rain started. (The rain was not walking!) ✓ Walking to school, I got caught in the rain.</p>\n<p>▸ Use whom (not who) directly after a preposition.</p>\n<p>▸ that is NOT used after a preposition or in non-defining clauses: ✗ the city in that …</p>\n<p>▸ -ing = active meaning; -ed / past participle = passive meaning.</p>\n<h3>Arabic Explanation</h3>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">شرح القاعدة بالعربية</span></strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">في الأسلوب الرسمي نضع حرف الجر قبل which أو whom، مثل the city in which I was born، ونستخدم whom للأشخاص بعد حرف الجر، ولا نستخدم that بعد حرف الجر.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">يمكن اختصار جملة الصلة: إذا كان المعنى مبنيًا للمعلوم نستخدم صيغة ing، مثل the girl talking to Huda، وإذا كان مبنيًا للمجهول نستخدم التصريف الثالث، مثل the cars made in Japan.</span></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">عند بدء الجملة بصيغة ing أو التصريف الثالث يجب أن يكون فاعلها هو فاعل الجملة الرئيسة، وإلا وقعنا في خطأ «الفاعل المعلّق»، ونستخدم Having + التصريف الثالث للحدث الأسبق.</span></p>\n<h3>Arab Learner Alert</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The house in that I live is old.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The house in which I live is old.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">لا نستخدم that بعد حرف الجر.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The man to who I spoke was kind.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The man to whom I spoke was kind.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد حرف الجر whom.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Walking home, the rain started.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Walking home, I got caught in the rain.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">فاعل ing يجب أن يكون فاعل الجملة الرئيسة.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>The books writing by Ibn Sina are famous.</em> <strong>→ ✓ The books written by Ibn Sina are famous.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المعنى مبني للمجهول فنستخدم التصريف الثالث.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>He has two sons, both of them are doctors.</em> <strong>→ ✓ He has two sons, both of whom are doctors.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">نستخدم of whom لربط الجملتين.</span></p>\n<p><strong>✗</strong> <em>Finished the work, he went home.</em> <strong>→ ✓ Having finished the work, he went home.</strong></p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">للحدث الأسبق Having + p.p.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Compare and Contrast</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Full: The man who is standing at the door is my uncle.</p>\n<p>Reduced (active): The man standing at the door is my uncle.</p>\n<p>Reduced (passive): The letter sent yesterday arrived today. (= which was sent)</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>STEP Strategy</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1. After a preposition: which (things) / whom (people), never that or who.</p>\n<p>2. For reduced clauses, ask: does the noun DO the action (-ing) or RECEIVE it (p.p.)?</p>\n<p>3. For a participle clause at the start, check that the main clause subject can do that action.</p>\n<p>4. Earlier completed action → Having + p.p.</p>\n<p>5. STEP traps: in that, to who, both of them (in a joined sentence), writing vs written.</p>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">بعد حرف الجر استخدم which أو whom، واختر ing إذا كان الاسم فاعلًا والتصريف الثالث إذا كان الحدث واقعًا عليه، وتأكد أن فاعل الجملة الفعلية في البداية هو فاعل الجملة الرئيسة.</span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3>Worked STEP Examples (not counted in the quiz)</h3>\n<p><strong>Example 1. The company employs 500 people, most of ______ work from home.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. them B. whom C. who D. which</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The sentence joins two clauses with a quantifier (most of).</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> For people after of → whom.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">most of whom للأشخاص.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 2. The dates ______ in Al-Qassim are famous across the Gulf.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. growing B. grown C. grow D. are grown</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The dates do not grow themselves in this sense; farmers grow them → passive.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Reduced passive relative → past participle.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> The answer is B.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">المعنى مبني للمجهول: grown.</span></p>\n<p><strong>Example 3. (A) <u>Arriving</u> late at the (B) <u>airport</u>, (C) <u>the plane</u> had (D) <u>already</u> left.</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>A. Arriving B. airport C. the plane D. already</p>\n<p><strong>Step 1:</strong> The person arriving late is not the plane.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2:</strong> This is a dangling participle; the subject must be the person.</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3:</strong> Correct: Arriving late at the airport, we found that the plane had already left. The answer is C.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p class=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\"><span dir=\"rtl\" lang=\"ar\">فاعل arriving يجب أن يكون الشخص لا الطائرة.</span></p>","wu":"Warm-up: 1 B · 2 A · 3 D · Worked examples: Example 1 B · Example 2 B · Example 3 C","quiz":[{"l":["Answer all 30 questions. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","أجب عن الأسئلة الثلاثين جميعها، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة من بين البدائل الأربعة.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–20): Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","الجزء الأول: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"This is the house in ______ my grandfather was born.","o":["that","which","where","whom"],"k":1,"e":"Preposition + which (thing).","h":"حرف جر + which."},{"n":2,"s":"The woman to ______ I gave the documents was very helpful.","o":["who","that","which","whom"],"k":3,"e":"Preposition + whom (person).","h":"حرف جر + whom."},{"n":3,"s":"The boy ______ in the front row is my cousin.","o":["sat","sits","sitting","who sitting"],"k":2,"e":"Reduced active relative → -ing.","h":"المعنى معلوم ing."},{"n":4,"s":"Most of the cars ______ in this factory are exported.","o":["making","make","made","which making"],"k":2,"e":"Reduced passive relative → past participle.","h":"المعنى مجهول p.p."},{"n":5,"s":"He has three daughters, all of ______ are teachers.","o":["them","whom","who","which"],"k":1,"e":"all of whom (people).","h":"all of whom."},{"n":6,"s":"______ tired, I went to bed early.","o":["Feeling","Felt","I felt","To feel"],"k":0,"e":"Participle clause of reason (active) → -ing.","h":"سبب بصيغة ing."},{"n":7,"s":"______ his homework, Turki went out to play.","o":["Finished","Having finished","Finishing already","Have finished"],"k":1,"e":"Earlier completed action → Having + p.p.","h":"حدث أسبق Having + p.p."},{"n":8,"s":"We visited five museums, two of ______ were closed.","o":["which","them","whom","that"],"k":0,"e":"Things + of which.","h":"of which للأشياء."},{"n":9,"s":"______ in 1865, the Masmak Fortress is now a museum.","o":["Building","Having built","Built","It built"],"k":2,"e":"Passive participle clause → Built.","h":"مبني للمجهول Built."},{"n":10,"s":"Anyone ______ to join the club should see Mr. Saleh.","o":["wanted","wants","who want","wanting"],"k":3,"e":"Reduced active relative → -ing.","h":"ing بمعنى who wants."},{"n":11,"s":"The topic on ______ we wrote our essays was very interesting.","o":["that","which","whom","what"],"k":1,"e":"Preposition + which.","h":"حرف جر + which."},{"n":12,"s":"The questions ______ in the interview were quite difficult.","o":["asked","asking","were asked","ask"],"k":0,"e":"Reduced passive → asked.","h":"المعنى مجهول."},{"n":13,"s":"______ along the beach, we saw a group of dolphins.","o":["Walked","We walked","To walking","Walking"],"k":3,"e":"Active participle clause with the same subject (we).","h":"ing بنفس الفاعل."},{"n":14,"s":"Ibn Sina, ______ books were studied for centuries, was born in 980.","o":["whose","who his","which","whom"],"k":0,"e":"Possession → whose.","h":"الملكية whose."},{"n":15,"s":"The students, most of ______ had studied hard, passed easily.","o":["them","which","who","whom"],"k":3,"e":"most of whom (people).","h":"most of whom."},{"n":16,"s":"______ by the news, she started to cry.","o":["Shocking","Having shocked","Shocked","She shocked"],"k":2,"e":"She was shocked (passive meaning) → Shocked.","h":"معنى مجهول Shocked."},{"n":17,"s":"The man with ______ I shared a taxi was a famous writer.","o":["whom","who","that","which"],"k":0,"e":"Preposition + whom.","h":"حرف جر + whom."},{"n":18,"s":"People ______ in hot countries often sleep in the afternoon.","o":["lived","live","are living","living"],"k":3,"e":"Reduced active relative → living.","h":"ing بمعنى who live."},{"n":19,"s":"Not ______ what to say, he remained silent.","o":["known","knew","to know","knowing"],"k":3,"e":"Negative participle clause of reason → Not knowing.","h":"Not + ing للسبب."},{"n":20,"s":"The bridge, ______ cost more than a billion riyals, opened last year.","o":["that","which","whose","what"],"k":1,"e":"Non-defining clause (commas) → which, not that.","h":"بعد الفاصلة which."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 21–30): Each sentence has four underlined parts (A, B, C, D). Choose the ONE part that is incorrect.","الجزء الثاني: في كل جملة أربعة أجزاء تحتها خط، اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"This is (A) the (B) school (C) at which my father (D) teach.","o":["the","school","at","teach"],"k":3,"e":"my father → teaches.","h":""},{"n":22,"s":"The (A) man (B) to who you (C) spoke (D) is my uncle.","o":["man","to who","spoke","is"],"k":1,"e":"Preposition + whom.","h":""},{"n":23,"s":"(A) The books writing by (B) this author (C) are (D) popular.","o":["The books writing","this","are","popular"],"k":0,"e":"Passive meaning → written.","h":""},{"n":24,"s":"He (A) has two (B) brothers, both of (C) them (D) work in Dammam.","o":["has","brothers","them","work"],"k":2,"e":"Joining clauses → both of whom.","h":""},{"n":25,"s":"(A) Walking (B) to school, (C) the rain (D) soaked my uniform.","o":["Walking","to","the rain","soaked"],"k":2,"e":"Dangling participle: the rain was not walking; the subject must be the person.","h":""},{"n":26,"s":"(A) Finished his work, the (B) engineer (C) went (D) home.","o":["Finished","engineer","went","home"],"k":0,"e":"Earlier action → Having finished.","h":""},{"n":27,"s":"The (A) city (B) in (C) that I (D) grew up has changed a lot.","o":["city","in","that","grew up"],"k":2,"e":"No that after a preposition.","h":""},{"n":28,"s":"The (A) girl (B) sat next to (C) me in class (D) is from Yemen.","o":["girl","sat","me","is"],"k":1,"e":"Reduced active relative → sitting.","h":""},{"n":29,"s":"(A) Surrounding by mountains, Abha (B) has a (C) cool (D) climate.","o":["Surrounding","has","cool","climate"],"k":0,"e":"Abha is surrounded (passive) → Surrounded.","h":""},{"n":30,"s":"We (A) visited ten (B) villages, most of (C) which (D) was very old.","o":["visited","villages","which","was"],"k":3,"e":"most of which (villages) is plural → were.","h":""}]}],"n":30}],"sc":{},"review":{"quiz":[{"l":["Unit Review — 50 questions. Questions 1–35: choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence. Questions 36–50: choose the ONE underlined part that is incorrect.","مراجعة الوحدة: خمسون سؤالًا؛ في الأسئلة من ١ إلى ٣٥ اختر الإجابة التي تكمل الجملة، وفي الأسئلة من ٣٦ إلى ٥٠ اختر الجزء الذي يحتوي على خطأ.","Part A — Sentence Completion (Questions 1–35)"],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"She was out of breath because she ______ for the bus.","o":["has been running","runs","had run since","had been running"],"k":3,"e":"Duration explaining a past result.","h":"تفسير نتيجة ماضية."},{"n":2,"s":"By the time the guests arrived, we ______ the house.","o":["have cleaned","cleaned already","had cleaned","were clean"],"k":2,"e":"Earlier completed action.","h":"حدث أسبق."},{"n":3,"s":"This time tomorrow, I ______ over the Red Sea.","o":["will fly at","will have flown","fly","will be flying"],"k":3,"e":"In progress at a future time.","h":"حدث مستمر مستقبلًا."},{"n":4,"s":"By 2030, the city ______ three new hospitals.","o":["will be opening","opens","will have opened","will open by"],"k":2,"e":"Completed by a future time.","h":"اكتمال قبل وقت مستقبلي."},{"n":5,"s":"If you had asked me, I ______ you the answer.","o":["would have given","would give","will give","had given"],"k":0,"e":"Third conditional result.","h":"الشرطية الثالثة."},{"n":6,"s":"Take some cash ______ the card machine doesn't work.","o":["unless","in case","provided","as long as"],"k":1,"e":"Precaution → in case.","h":"احتياط."},{"n":7,"s":"I wish I ______ the train this morning. Now I'm late.","o":["hadn't missed","didn't miss","wouldn't miss","don't miss"],"k":0,"e":"Past regret.","h":"ندم على الماضي."},{"n":8,"s":"It's time we ______ a decision.","o":["make","will make","made","had made"],"k":2,"e":"It's time + subject + past simple.","h":"It's time مع الماضي."},{"n":9,"s":"We had our air conditioner ______ last week.","o":["service","servicing","to service","serviced"],"k":3,"e":"Causative: had + object + p.p.","h":"السببي."},{"n":10,"s":"It ______ that the new airport will be the biggest in the region.","o":["expects","is expected","is expecting","expected it"],"k":1,"e":"Impersonal passive.","h":"مبني للمجهول غير شخصي."},{"n":11,"s":"The teacher reminded us ______ our ID cards.","o":["bringing","bring","to bring","for bringing"],"k":2,"e":"remind + object + to.","h":"remind + مفعول + to."},{"n":12,"s":"He admitted ______ the rules.","o":["to break","breaking","break","that break"],"k":1,"e":"admit + -ing.","h":"admit مع ing."},{"n":13,"s":"The road is wet. It ______ while we were sleeping.","o":["must rain","must have rained","should have rained","can't rain"],"k":1,"e":"Past deduction.","h":"استنتاج ماضٍ."},{"n":14,"s":"You ______ me. I would have helped you.","o":["must have called","should call","can't have called","should have called"],"k":3,"e":"Criticism → should have.","h":"لوم."},{"n":15,"s":"The report on ______ the decision was based was very long.","o":["that","whom","which","what"],"k":2,"e":"Preposition + which.","h":"حرف جر + which."},{"n":16,"s":"The bags ______ at the airport were sent to the wrong city.","o":["losing","lose","were lost","lost"],"k":3,"e":"Reduced passive relative.","h":"اختصار مبني للمجهول."},{"n":17,"s":"Just as I ______ asleep, the phone rang.","o":["had fallen","have fallen","was falling","fall"],"k":2,"e":"Action in progress interrupted.","h":"حدث مستمر قُطع."},{"n":18,"s":"Don't call between 4 and 6. I ______ an online lesson.","o":["will be teaching","will have taught","teach","will teach at"],"k":0,"e":"In progress during a future period.","h":"حدث مستمر."},{"n":19,"s":"If I had studied engineering, I ______ in a factory now.","o":["would be working","would have worked","will work","worked"],"k":0,"e":"Mixed conditional (now).","h":"شرطية مختلطة."},{"n":20,"s":"I'd rather you ______ me before visiting.","o":["call","will call","called","to call"],"k":2,"e":"would rather + another subject + past simple.","h":"مع فاعل آخر الماضي."},{"n":21,"s":"The pyramids are thought ______ by thousands of workers.","o":["to have been built","to build","being built","that built"],"k":0,"e":"Personal passive, earlier action.","h":"حدث سابق مبني للمجهول."},{"n":22,"s":"The officer warned the drivers ______ too fast.","o":["don't drive","not to drive","not driving","to not driving"],"k":1,"e":"warn + object + not to.","h":"warn + not to."},{"n":23,"s":"She ______ the message. Her phone was broken.","o":["mustn't have read","should have read","needn't read","can't have read"],"k":3,"e":"Negative past deduction.","h":"استنتاج منفي ماضٍ."},{"n":24,"s":"______ the test, the students handed in their papers.","o":["Having completed","Completed","Have completed","Completing already"],"k":0,"e":"Earlier action → Having + p.p.","h":"Having + p.p."},{"n":25,"s":"They ______ in Tabuk for five years when they moved to Riyadh.","o":["had been living","have been living","lived since","were live"],"k":0,"e":"Duration before a past event.","h":"مدة قبل حدث ماضٍ."},{"n":26,"s":"By next June, my sister ______ her degree.","o":["will be completing since","will have completed","completes","has completed"],"k":1,"e":"Completed by a future time.","h":"اكتمال قبل وقت مستقبلي."},{"n":27,"s":"You can borrow my notes ______ you give them back tomorrow.","o":["provided that","unless","in case","even though"],"k":0,"e":"On condition → provided that.","h":"بشرط."},{"n":28,"s":"If only I ______ more confident in interviews!","o":["am","will be","were","had been yesterday"],"k":2,"e":"Present wish → were.","h":"أمنية حاضرة."},{"n":29,"s":"I'm going to get my car ______ before the trip.","o":["check","checking","to check","checked"],"k":3,"e":"get + object + p.p.","h":"get + المفعول + p.p."},{"n":30,"s":"The manager insisted ______ the meeting on Sunday.","o":["on holding","to hold","holding","for holding"],"k":0,"e":"insist on + -ing.","h":"insist on + ing."},{"n":31,"s":"We ______ the tickets in advance. The stadium was half empty.","o":["didn't need buy","mustn't have bought","can't have bought","needn't have bought"],"k":3,"e":"Done but unnecessary.","h":"فعلناه دون حاجة."},{"n":32,"s":"The new students, most of ______ come from abroad, need help with Arabic.","o":["them","whom","who","which"],"k":1,"e":"most of whom (people).","h":"most of whom."},{"n":33,"s":"We'll miss the start of the show ______ we leave now.","o":["if","in case","as long as","unless"],"k":3,"e":"Except if we leave now → unless.","h":"unless = إلا إذا."},{"n":34,"s":"Experts recommend ______ the car serviced twice a year.","o":["to have","having","us to have","have"],"k":1,"e":"recommend + -ing (with a causative).","h":"recommend مع ing."},{"n":35,"s":"I wish my brother ______ his music so loud at night.","o":["wouldn't play","doesn't play","won't play","didn't played"],"k":0,"e":"Annoyance → wish + would.","h":"انزعاج wish + would."}]},{"l":["Part B — Error Identification (Questions 36–50)"],"q":[{"n":36,"s":"When I (A) arrived, the (B) film (C) already (D) started.","o":["arrived","film","already","started"],"k":2,"e":"Earlier action → had already started.","h":""},{"n":37,"s":"(A) By the time you will come, (B) we (C) will have (D) finished.","o":["By the time you will come","we","will have","finished"],"k":0,"e":"After by the time → present simple.","h":""},{"n":38,"s":"If (A) she had (B) listened to me, she (C) wouldn't (D) make that mistake.","o":["she","listened","wouldn't","make"],"k":3,"e":"Third conditional → wouldn't have made.","h":""},{"n":39,"s":"I (A) wish I (B) would (C) know the (D) answer.","o":["wish","would","know","answer"],"k":1,"e":"No would for yourself.","h":""},{"n":40,"s":"We (A) had the (B) windows (C) clean (D) yesterday.","o":["had","windows","clean","yesterday"],"k":2,"e":"have + object + p.p.","h":""},{"n":41,"s":"He (A) suggested (B) us (C) to (D) take a taxi.","o":["suggested","us","to","take"],"k":1,"e":"suggest cannot take object + to.","h":""},{"n":42,"s":"(A) She must have went (B) home; her (C) bag is (D) gone.","o":["She must have went","home","bag","gone"],"k":0,"e":"must have + gone.","h":""},{"n":43,"s":"The (A) man (B) to who I (C) gave the (D) keys was the manager.","o":["man","to who","gave","keys"],"k":1,"e":"Preposition + whom.","h":""},{"n":44,"s":"At (A) midnight tonight, most (B) of us (C) will (D) sleep.","o":["midnight","of","will","sleep"],"k":3,"e":"In progress at a future time → will be sleeping.","h":""},{"n":45,"s":"My (A) brother was (B) tired because he (C) worked in the garden (D) for hours.","o":["brother","tired","worked","for hours"],"k":2,"e":"Duration explaining a past result → had been raining.","h":""},{"n":46,"s":"(A) Unless you don't book now, (B) there (C) won't be any (D) seats left.","o":["Unless you don't","there","won't","seats"],"k":0,"e":"unless already means if not.","h":""},{"n":47,"s":"It's (A) about time we (B) start (C) planning the (D) trip.","o":["about","start","planning","trip"],"k":1,"e":"It's time + subject + past simple.","h":""},{"n":48,"s":"The (A) castle (B) is (C) said (D) that it was built in 1200.","o":["castle","is","said","that it was built"],"k":3,"e":"Subject + is said + to have been + p.p.","h":""},{"n":49,"s":"(A) They accused (B) the (C) driver (D) for causing the accident.","o":["They accused","the","driver","for causing"],"k":3,"e":"accuse somebody of + -ing.","h":""},{"n":50,"s":"You (A) shouldn't (B) have (C) to leave the door (D) open.","o":["shouldn't","have","to leave","open"],"k":2,"e":"shouldn't have + past participle.","h":""}]}],"n":50}};
